window.RBT_EXAMS = [{"id": "exam1", "title": "Examen 1", "questions": [{"q": "Which of the following would be best at tracking frequency?", "opts": ["A stopwatch", "Your hand", "Counting in your head", "A clicker counter"], "ans": 3, "ex": "La frecuencia cuenta cada vez que ocurre una conducta. Un contador (clicker) permite registrar cada instancia sin perder la cuenta. El cronómetro mide tiempo, y contar 'en la cabeza' o 'con la mano' es poco preciso y se pierde fácilmente."}, {"q": "You are recording how long it takes your client to get dressed in the morning. What type of data are you taking?", "opts": ["Frequency", "IRT", "Duration", "Latency"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Mides cuánto DURA la conducta (el tiempo para vestirse): eso es duración. Frecuencia cuenta las veces, IRT es el tiempo entre respuestas y latencia es el tiempo entre la orden y la respuesta."}, {"q": "Billy's mom gave him a list of items to buy at the grocery store while Billy's mom was at work. When she returned home, she checked to make sure Billy had bought all of the items on the list. What type of data collection is this?", "opts": ["Permanent Product", "Frequency", "IRT", "Rate"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Verificar después si Billy compró todo lo de la lista es producto permanente: mides el RESULTADO de la conducta, no la conducta en vivo. La lista funciona como registro del producto."}, {"q": "Your role in a functional assessment as an RBT is?", "opts": ["To criticize the assessment", "To assist with the assessment", "To conduct the assessment", "To standy by and do nothing"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El RBT apoya el proceso: el análisis funcional (funcional assessment) lo diseña y conduce el supervisor. Tu papel es asistir y tomar datos, nunca diseñar ni decidir el análisis por tu cuenta."}, {"q": "What is your primary role as an RBT?", "opts": ["Treatment planning", "Preference assessment", "Parent training", "Implementation"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Tu función primaria es IMPLEMENTAR los programas diseñados por el BCBA bajo supervisión. No diseñas planes, ni haces análisis funcionales, ni entrenas a otros por tu cuenta."}, {"q": "Which of the following behaviors is defined in the most observable and measurable terms?", "opts": ["Susie snapper her pencil in half after she incorrectly answered the math problem", "Susie was angry so she snapped her pencil in half", "Susie snapped her pencil in half because she has autism", "Susie's anxiety caused her to snap her pencil in half"], "ans": 0, "ex": "'Rompió el lápiz en dos' es observable y medible. Las emociones (enojada), diagnósticos (autismo) o estados internos (ansiedad) no se pueden ver ni medir directamente."}, {"q": "You want to decrease the time it takes your client to eat their meal. You are told to record the length of time in between bites. What kind of data are you collecting?", "opts": ["Duration", "Total task", "IRT", "Latency"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El tiempo entre un bocado y el siguiente es IRT (tiempo entre respuestas). La duración sería todo el tiempo de la comida; la frecuencia contaría los bocados."}, {"q": "What is the difference between frequency and rate?", "opts": ["Rate is frequency with a time component added", "Rate requires duration data", "There is no difference between the two", "Rate is more accurate than frequency"], "ans": 0, "ex": "La tasa incluye el TIEMPO (veces por minuto/hora); la frecuencia es solo el número de veces. Ambos cuentan ocurrencias, pero la tasa divide entre el tiempo."}, {"q": "Before you can start collecting data, what is the first thing that should be done?", "opts": ["Collect your required materials", "Define the target behavior", "Report to your supervisor", "Select a data collection method"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Lo primero es definir la conducta objetivo en términos observables y medibles. Sin definición no puedes saber qué registrar ni cuándo contar."}, {"q": "What type of interval recording underestimates the occurrence of behavior?", "opts": ["Partial interval", "Whole interval", "Momentary time sampling", "Frequency"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El registro de intervalo completo SUBESTIMA: exige que la conducta ocurra durante todo el intervalo para contarla. El registro parcial tiende a sobreestimar."}, {"q": "Which of the following is a type of discontinuous measurement?", "opts": ["Frequency", "Rate", "Duration", "Partial interval recording"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Son medidas discontinuas: registro de intervalo parcial, completo y muestreo de tiempo momentáneo. Frecuencia, duración, latencia y tasa son continuas."}, {"q": "What is the goal of a preference assessment?", "opts": ["Find out what is reinforcing to the client", "Determine punishers for the individual", "Identify stimuli that may be motivating", "Allow the client to choose what they want to work on during session"], "ans": 2, "ex": "La evaluación de preferencias identifica y ordena reforzadores (lo que le gusta al cliente) para usarlos después. No evalúa habilidades ni selecciona programas."}, {"q": "You are teaching your client to say \"bubble.\" Your client says \"b\" and you deliver reinforcement. Next time your client says \"b\" you don't deliver reinforcement. Instead, you waituntil your client says \"bub\". You repeat this process and slowly increase the requirements for reinforcement up until your client says \"bubble.\" What are you implementing?", "opts": ["Shaping", "Task chaining", "FCT", "Punishment"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Es modelado (shaping): refuerzas aproximaciones sucesivas al objetivo ('b' → 'bub' → 'bubble'). Cada vez exiges una respuesta más parecida a la meta."}, {"q": "You are trying to teach your client to wash your hands. Your BCBA instructs you to use backwards chaining to teach this. What step might you teach first?", "opts": ["Turning the water on", "Putting soap on their hands", "Drying their hands off with a towel", "Entering the bathroom"], "ans": 2, "ex": "En encadenamiento hacia atrás enseñas el ÚLTIMO paso primero (el paso final de lavarse las manos), y retrocedes por la cadena. Lo primero que se enseña es el paso final."}, {"q": "A student stands up and walks around the room at inappropriate times. You decide you are going to deliver reinforcement on a FI-3 reinforcement schedule for the student sitting in their chair. If the student gets up and walks around no reinforcement is delivered. What type of procedure is this?", "opts": ["DRI", "DRO", "DRA", "DRL"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Refuerzas una conducta alternativa (sentarse) y retiras el refuerzo de la conducta problema: es reforzamiento diferencial (DRA). El FI-3 indica cuándo hay refuerzo disponible."}, {"q": "Your client screams for extended periods of time throughout the day. Your BCBA instructs youto deliver reinforcement any time the client is not screaming. What type of procedure is this?", "opts": ["DRI", "DRO", "DRA", "DRH"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Reforzar CUALQUIER momento en que NO grita es DRO (reforzamiento diferencial de otras conductas): la ausencia de la conducta objetivo recibe refuerzo."}, {"q": "Linda elopes from the table when presented with a lengthy task. You start functional communication training with Linda in hopes you can teach her to ask for a break. Now, whenever Linda asks for a break when presented with a lengthy task, you provide reinforcement. What type of reinforcement procedure is this?", "opts": ["DRI", "DRO", "DRD", "DRA"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Enseñas a Linda a PEDIR un descanso y la petición recibe refuerzo (conducta alternativa); la conducta problema deja de funcionar. Es reforzamiento diferencial/comunicación funcional."}, {"q": "In this type of teaching there is an antecedent, a behavior, a consequence, and a brief pause before the next antecedent", "opts": ["NET", "FCT", "Prompting", "DTT"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Esa estructura (antecedente → conducta → consecuencia → pausa breve) describe el ensayo discreto (DTT): así se estructura cada ensayo de enseñanza."}, {"q": "When should you deliver a prompt?", "opts": ["After the consequence", "Before the SD", "After the response", "After the SD, before the response"], "ans": 3, "ex": "La ayuda (prompt) se entrega de inmediato, ANTES de que el cliente se equivoque, para asegurar la respuesta correcta. No esperas a que falle para responder."}, {"q": "Billy has soccer practice today. When it's time to leave, Billy's dad tells Billy to grab his soccerbag. Billy complies and grabs his stuff. His dad says \"Nice job. Let's load up the car.\" In this scenario, what is the antecedent to Billy grabbing his stuff?", "opts": ["Billy has soccer practice today", "There is no clear antecedent", "Billy's dad telling Billy to grab his soccer bag", "\"Nice job. Let's load up the car.\""], "ans": 2, "ex": "El antecedente es lo que ocurre antes de la conducta: la orden del papá ('toma tu bolso') que hace probable la respuesta. La consecuencia (elogio) viene después."}, {"q": "The process of breaking down a skill into smaller, more manageable components by doing the task yourself, or watching someone else do the task, is called?", "opts": ["Task analysis", "Task chaining", "Forward Chaining", "DTT"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Romper una habilidad en pasos pequeños observando cómo se hace es un análisis de tarea (task analysis). Es la base para enseñar cadenas conductuales."}, {"q": "You have been working with your client for two years. Your client's mom tells you they are going out with friends tomorrow and offers to pay you to babysit. If you accepted, what would you be violating?", "opts": ["Dual relationships", "Respondinga appropriately to feedback", "Legal compliance", "Effective communication"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Aceptar el pago para cuidar al cliente fuera del horario crea una relación dual/conflicto de interés (relación financiera personal con la familia). Eso viola la ética."}, {"q": "Your session takes place during lunch time each day. The client's parents have started to buy you lunch and requested you eat lunch with them each day. What is the best course of action?", "opts": ["Eat lunch with the family", "Politely decline and inform your supervisor", "Get rid of the client", "Change the session time"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Aceptar que los padres le compren el almuerzo cada día crea una relación dual. Lo correcto es agradecer y DECLINAR cortésmente para mantener los límites profesionales."}, {"q": "During proper discrimination training, reinforcement is available for one response, but not for another. Which of the following is an example of discrimination training?", "opts": ["Shoe tying", "You praise your client when they put on their pants independently", "You tell your client to touch \"blue.\" You deliver reinforcement when your cilent touches blue, but not when he touches green", "Your client has started calling all animals \"dogs\""], "ans": 2, "ex": "En el entrenamiento en discriminación, la respuesta correcta recibe refuerzo ante un estímulo (SD) y NO ante otro (SΔ). El ejemplo muestra cómo se aprende a distinguir."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an example of generalization?", "opts": ["You teach your client to make purchases at the clinic. Now, your client is able to buy his own lunch at school", "Your client will have a conversation with the math teacher, but not any of his other teachers", "Your client has learned to count to", "You ask your client to touch the \"blue\" card. They touch the green card"], "ans": 0, "ex": "La generalización: la conducta aprendida ocurre en condiciones o entornos nuevos además del de entrenamiento. Es la meta natural de la enseñanza."}, {"q": "When explaining something to parents what should you try and do?", "opts": ["Use technical language and jargon", "Never explain anything to parents", "Record every conversation you have with parents", "Use terminology that the parent is able to understand"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Habla con lenguaje claro y SIN jerga técnica (evita términos como 'reforzador', 'SD'). Las familias deben entender sin tecnicismos."}, {"q": "Bobby is working with a client in-home. The client's mom wants the client to be able to prepare their own breakfast. Bobby teaches the client to make scrambled eggs using a task chain procedure. Bobby helps the client by getting out the plate and utensils. The client turns on the stove, heats the pan, puts butter in the pan, cracks the eggs in the pan, scrambles the eggs, puts them on a plate, and turns off the stove. One day, Bobby does not put out the plate. What is he implementing?", "opts": ["Forward chaining", "Behavior Chain Interruption Strategy (BCIS)", "Task analysis", "Fading"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Al retirar el plato y los utensilios (material ya preparado), Bobby desvanece una ayuda de estímulo para que la conducta quede bajo los estímulos naturales."}, {"q": "Tangible, automatic, attention, and escape are?", "opts": ["Irrelevant to ABA", "Mentalisms", "The four functions of behavior", "A type of punishment"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Las cuatro funciones de la conducta: atención, escape/evitación, tangible (acceso) y automática/sensorial. Identificar la función guía el tratamiento."}, {"q": "Joe is in the kitchen doing a puzzle with his mom. Joe's brother needs help completing his math homework, and asks his mom for assistance. Joe's mom gets up and goes help the brother. Five minutes later, Joe starts banging his fists on the table. Hypothetically, what function might this serve?", "opts": ["Anger", "Escape", "Tangible", "Attention"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Joe golpea la mesa cuando mamá atiende a su hermano: la conducta le consigue la ATENCIÓN de su mamá (ella vuelve o lo atiende). Función: atención."}, {"q": "Which of the following is a response prompt?", "opts": ["Verbal", "Modeling", "Full physical", "All of the above"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Una ayuda de respuesta evoca la conducta en sí (verbal, gestual, modelado o física). Las ayudas de estímulo modifican el ambiente en vez de guiar la respuesta."}, {"q": "The behavior results in the addition of something that increases the behavior in the future. What does this describe?", "opts": ["Negative Reinforcement", "Positive Reinforcement", "Positive Punishment", "Negative Punishment"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Reforzamiento positivo: se AGREGA algo (el refuerzo) y aumenta la conducta en el futuro. 'Adición + aumento' = positivo."}, {"q": "Every time Alex yells out in class he is sent to the principal's office. This goes on for two weeks, and Alex's yelling increases. What is happening in this scenario?", "opts": ["Alex's behavior is being reinforced", "Alex's behavior is being punished", "It cannot be determined", "Alex's behavior is being put on extinction"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Alex grita → lo mandan a la oficina (se agrega algo) → el grito AUMENTA: es reforzamiento positivo, aunque el resultado parezca un castigo."}, {"q": "During the night, Joanne gets out of bed to ask mom to get her a snack. In the past, mom hascomplied and given Joanne a granola bar. For the past week, when Joanne asks for a snack, mom has not given her one. What is Joanne's mom implementing?", "opts": ["Extinction", "Negative reinforcement", "Response blocking", "Punishment"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Dejar de darle la granola bar cuando pide es EXTINCIÓN: se retira el refuerzo que mantenía la conducta. La conducta de pedir deja de funcionar."}, {"q": "Extinction requires what?", "opts": ["Withholding some reinforcement", "Witholding all reinforcement", "Proper implementation only some of the time", "Punishment"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La extinción requiere identificar y RETIRAR el refuerzo que mantiene la conducta y mantenerse consistente. Sin identificación del refuerzo no hay extinción."}, {"q": "A BCBA instructs the RBT to put all attention-seeking behavior on extinction. In order to gain attention, the client will tap their pencil on the table. During extinction, the tapping has gotten more intense and is occurring more frequently. Yesterday, the client tapped the pencil so hardthat the pencil broke. What is most likely occurring?", "opts": ["The RBT is violating the ethical code", "An extinction burst", "The client is angry", "Poor implementation of the procedure"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El aumento temporal de intensidad y frecuencia al suspender el refuerzo es un estallido de extinción (extinction burst). Es esperado y no significa que falle el plan."}, {"q": "What is the most common graph used in ABA?", "opts": ["A pie chart", "A histogram", "A line graph", "A scatterplot"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El gráfico de línea (line graph) es el más usado en ABA para mostrar el cambio de la conducta a lo largo de sesiones o tiempo."}, {"q": "What is the primary difference between Discrete Trial Training and Incidental Teaching", "opts": ["Incidental teaching doesn't use reinforcement", "Incidental teaching occurs in the natural environment", "There is no difference", "DTT is better than incidental teaching"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El DTT es estructurado, dirigido por el terapeuta y en mesa; la enseñanza incidental (NET) es naturalista, iniciada por el aprendiz y en el ambiente real."}, {"q": "Which of the following describes a contingency?", "opts": ["Increases behavior", "An if-then statement", "A punishment procedure", "A way to measure how long something takes"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Una contingencia es la relación 'si... entonces...': si ocurre la conducta, entonces viene la consecuencia. Define qué conducta produce qué resultado."}, {"q": "Which of the following reinforcement schedules is based on an average number of correct responses?", "opts": ["FR2", "FI3", "VR3", "DRO"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El programa de razón variable (VR) refuerza después de un número PROMEDIO de respuestas correctas. El intervalo se basa en tiempo, no en respuestas."}, {"q": "RBTs should record session notes:", "opts": ["Each session", "Weekly", "Monthly", "Yearly"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Las notas de sesión se registran DESPUÉS DE CADA sesión (la misma sesión), no semanal ni mensualmente."}, {"q": "You are struggling with a client. Who is the first person you should contact?", "opts": ["The parent", "Your supervisor/BCBA", "The company's director", "The authorities"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Ante dificultades con un cliente, el primer contacto es tu BCBA/supervisor. Si el problema es urgente, también puedes recurrir a otro miembro del equipo, pero siempre empieza por tu supervisor."}, {"q": "Which of the following is a requirement for session notes:", "opts": ["The notes are your personal opinion", "The notes are objective", "You document how the client slept last night", "What they client ate for lunch"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Las notas de sesión deben ser objetivas, profesionales y basadas en datos. No llevan opiniones ni lenguaje subjetivo."}, {"q": "You are recording the time it takes from the presentation of the demand (SD) to the first instance of behavior. What are you measuring?", "opts": ["Duration", "Frequency", "Latency", "IRT"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Mides el tiempo desde la presentación del SD hasta la PRIMERA respuesta: eso es latencia. La duración mide cuánto dura la conducta."}, {"q": "Examples are food, water, sleep", "opts": ["Secondary reinforcers", "Consequences", "Primary reinforcers", "SD"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Comida, agua y sueño son reforzadores INCONDICIONADOS: su valor es biológico, no requiere aprendizaje. Los condicionados (dinero, elogios, fichas) se aprenden."}, {"q": "What comes before the behavior?", "opts": ["Consequence", "Response", "Antecedent", "Punishment"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El antecedente es lo que ocurre ANTES de la conducta. La conducta es lo que hace la persona y la consecuencia viene después."}, {"q": "Select the best definition for differential reinforcement from the choices below:", "opts": ["A stimulus, that when presented following a bx, causes an overall INCREASE in that bx over time", "Providing greater reinforcement for better approximations of a target behavior, and placing other behaviors on extinction or on a less desirable reinforcement schedule", "A stimulus that signals the availability of a reinforcer", "A stimulus that, when presented following a behavior, causes an overall DECREASE in that behavior over time"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Reforzamiento diferencial: refuerzas una conducta (o clase) y NO refuerzas otra. Así la conducta reforzada aumenta y la otra se reduce."}, {"q": "Freezing temperatures and electric shocks are examples of what type of punisher?", "opts": ["Conditioned", "Positive", "Unconditioned", "Negative"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Temperaturas heladas y descargas eléctricas son castigadores INCONDICIONADOS: son aversivos por naturaleza, sin necesidad de aprendizaje previo."}, {"q": "If you believe your client is being abused, which of the following should you do?", "opts": ["Contact relevant authorities", "Follow organization policies", "Consult with your supervisor", "All of the above"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Ante sospecha de abuso, tu deber es REPORTAR a las autoridades correspondientes (y a tu supervisor). El RBT es reportante obligatorio."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an antecedent technique?", "opts": ["Prompting", "DRA", "Task Analysis", "Punishment"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Una técnica de antecedente modifica el ambiente ANTES de la conducta para prevenirla o facilitar otra (dar opciones, modificar demandas, NCR)."}, {"q": "A repertoire refers to?", "opts": ["The skills a client possesses", "A type of antecdent intervention", "A verbal operant", "The type of measurement you are using"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El repertorio es el conjunto total de conductas y habilidades que la persona puede realizar. Define lo que ya sabe hacer."}, {"q": "Another word for request is?", "opts": ["Tact", "Intraverbal", "Mand", "Echoic"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El mand es la petición/request: la conducta que pide algo (el reforzador). 'Quiero agua' es un mand."}, {"q": "Every time you say \"put on your shoes\" your daughter says \"put on your shoes\". What type of verbal operant is this?", "opts": ["Mand", "Echoic", "Tact", "Intraverbal"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Repetir lo que otro dice es un ECOICO (ecoico): imitar el habla. La hija repite la palabra justo después de oírla."}, {"q": "Susie's family is driving down the road when they pass by a farm. Susie looks out the window and says \"cow.\" How would you describe Susie saying cow?", "opts": ["Manding", "Tacting", "Protesting", "Scripting"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Decir 'vaca' al VER una vaca es un tacto: etiquetar un estímulo del ambiente, sin necesidad de preguntar antes."}, {"q": "Johnny's teacher says \"OK, class who can tell me what 2+2 is\". Johnny responds with \"4!\" What verbal operant does this describe?", "opts": ["Mand", "Intraverbal", "Tact", "Autoclitic"], "ans": 1, "ex": "'¿Cuánto es 2+2?' → '¡4!' es un intraverbal: responder con palabras a otras palabras (conversación, preguntas)."}, {"q": "What are you measuring when you take permanent product data?", "opts": ["Intensity", "Production", "Length of time", "You aren't measuring anything"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El producto permanente mide el RESULTADO que deja la conducta (trabajo hecho, lista completa), no la conducta mientras ocurre."}, {"q": "At the end of session, Ralph's grandma asks how session went and for updates on progress. Which of the following is an inappropriate way to describe the day?", "opts": ["\"Ralph only eloped two times today! He was compliant and we were able to hit all his targets.\"", "\"I don't think it went well. I don't think my BCBA's plan is working.\"", "\"Session went smoothly today. My BCBA said she implemented a task chain for showering indepedently in the morning. How is that going?\"", "\"He is making progress. Today we worked on communication and self-help\""], "ans": 1, "ex": "Decir que 'el plan del BCBA no está funcionando' es subjetivo y desprofesional, y ventilar detalles del caso con la abuela también es inapropiado. Hay que ser objetivo y positivo."}, {"q": "During session your client's mom asks you to train them on DTT. What is the best response?", "opts": ["Inform the parent that you'll let your BCBA know of their desire to be trained as you aren't allowed to train by yourself", "Train the parent yourself", "Explain to the parent that parents aren't allowed to be trained", "Panic"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El RBT no entrena a los padres por su cuenta: la respuesta correcta es dirigir la petición al BCBA, que es quien supervisa el entrenamiento."}, {"q": "Your 21 year old client smokes cigarettes. Your BCBA decides that smoking is bad for your client and implements a program to decrease smoking without consulting the client first. Is thisappropriate?", "opts": ["No, the client is not breaking any laws and has the right to be consulted with before decisions are made", "Yes, smoking is unhealthy. The BCBA is protecting their client", "Yes, BCBAs are allowed to make any changes they want without consulting the client", "No, it is unclear if smoking is unhealthy"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Disminuir el consumo de cigarrillos de un cliente adulto SIN consultarle NO es apropiado. El RBT respeta la autonomía/consentimiento del cliente."}, {"q": "Rebecca's BCBA designs a complex behavior plan that involves multiple steps and procedures. During the first session that the behavior plan is implemented, Rebecca reinforces the wrong behavior. What should she do?", "opts": ["Pretend it didn't happen", "She just needs to put it in her notes without telling anyone", "Report herself to the parents", "Tell her supervisor/BCBA immediately and request more training"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Si refuerzas la conducta equivocada, no lo ocultes: informa a tu BCBA de inmediato. El supervisor corrige el plan y restablece la fidelidad."}, {"q": "Which of the following examples would be acceptable in a session note?", "opts": ["\"The client was angry with me today which is why behaviors occured\"", "\"Nothing significant happened today\"", "\"The client became anxious when I told him to grab his cup from the kitchen\"", "\"The client manded 8 times today indendently. The client also tacted \"spoon\" and \"fork\""], "ans": 3, "ex": "La nota correcta es la OBJETIVA y factual, basada en datos observables. Las opiniones, juicios y suposiciones no van en las notas."}, {"q": "A crisis/emergency situation is:", "opts": ["Not a big deal", "A situation where you, the client, or someone else is in danger", "Something you should not report to your supervisor", "Only happens with older clients"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Una crisis/emergencia es una situación súbita de conducta o salud que requiere actuación inmediata y el protocolo del equipo (seguridad primero)."}, {"q": "Which of the following increases or decreases the value of a reinforcer", "opts": ["Motivating operation", "Abolishing operation", "Discriminative Stimuli", "SD"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El EO/MO (operación motivadora) altera el VALOR de un reforzador (por ejemplo, el hambre hace más valiosa la comida). El SD solo señala disponibilidad."}, {"q": "You are teaching a child to write their name. You start by having them trace bold, large letters.You then remove the bold and have them trace the letters. You then make the letters normal size and have them trace. You then remove the beginning two letters of their name and have them trace. You then remove all letters and have them write their name independently. What are you doing?", "opts": ["Prompt fading", "Task chaining", "DTT", "Verbal prompting"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Desvaneces ayudas de manera gradual (letras grandes y negras → trazos → tamaño normal → independiente). Es desvanecimiento de estímulo/transferencia de control."}, {"q": "What type of reinforcement system is based on time?", "opts": ["Ratio", "DRI", "Interval", "DRA"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Un sistema de reforzamiento BASA EN EL TIEMPO es el intervalo (intervalo fijo o variable): el refuerzo llega según el tiempo, no según respuestas."}, {"q": "Which of the following is not a type of continuous measurement?", "opts": ["Latency", "Duration", "Frequency", "Partial time sampling"], "ans": 3, "ex": "No es medida continua el registro de intervalo (parcial, completo) ni el muestreo momentáneo: son medidas discontinuas porque muestrean el tiempo."}, {"q": "Ethically and professionally, you should comply with what? Pick the best answer", "opts": ["You only need to comply with the law", "All legal, regulatory, and workplace requirements", "Company policy", "The ethical code"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Cumples con las directrices de tu supervisor/BCBA y con el Código de Ética, sin importar preferencias personales. Ambas son obligatorias."}, {"q": "What question should you ask yourself when presented with an ethical dilemma?", "opts": ["What's the right thing to do?", "What's worth doing?", "What does it mean to be a good RBT?", "All of these"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Ante un dilema ético te preguntas por el bienestar del CLIENTE: '¿Está esto en el mejor interés del cliente?' Todo lo demás es secundario."}, {"q": "You are bitten by a mosquito. The bite starts to itch, so you scratch it. Scratching the itch is what?", "opts": ["Negative reinforcement", "Positive reinforcement", "Negative punishment", "Positive punishment"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Rascarse quita el picor (estímulo aversivo que se RETIRA) y por eso aumenta: es reforzamiento negativo (remoción que aumenta la conducta)."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an example of a prompt?", "opts": ["Turning on your computer", "Writing a note to remind your partner to take out the trash", "Compying with an instruction", "Opening a window when you are hot"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Una ayuda/prompt es un estímulo añadido ANTES de la conducta que asegura la respuesta correcta (verbal, gestual, física, etc.)."}, {"q": "Every day you put your key in the ignition, turn it, and your car starts. Today, your car doesn't start. You begin to aggressively turn the key, push the gas pedal, and pound the steering wheel. What might be happening?", "opts": ["An extinction burst", "Punishment", "Avoidance behavior", "Tacting"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El auto no arranca y aumentas la fuerza/frecuencia de intentos: es un estallido de extinción, porque la respuesta reforzada antes deja de funcionar."}, {"q": "What is the best reinforcement schedule for teaching a new skill?", "opts": ["VR2", "FR1", "FR6", "FI2"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Para ENSEÑAR una habilidad nueva se usa refuerzo continuo (FR1: cada respuesta correcta): así se establece rápido la conducta. El intermitente sirve para mantenerla."}, {"q": "What reinforcement schedule is the most productive and resistant to extinction?", "opts": ["FR", "FI", "VI", "VR"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El programa de razón variable (VR) produce la conducta más resistente a la extinción y una tasa alta. No hay patrón predecible."}, {"q": "What is not an example of discrimination?", "opts": ["Identifying different colors in a crayon box", "Calling all women you see \"mom\"", "Ordering coke instead of sprite", "Using a $5 bill instead of a $1 bill"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La discriminación es responder distinto ante estímulos diferentes. Responder IGUAL ante todos (generalizar) NO es discriminación."}, {"q": "Reinforcement can be continuous or intermittent. Behavior on what type of schedule is the hardest to extinguish?", "opts": ["Intermittent", "FR1", "Continuous", "Parent designed"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Lo más difícil de extinguir es lo reforzado de forma INTERMITENTE (variable): la persona nunca sabe cuándo vendrá el refuerzo y sigue respondiendo."}, {"q": "When we refer to baseline data we are referring to?", "opts": ["Data taken after intervention starts", "Data taken before intervention is put in place", "Data taken in the morning", "Data taken by the parent"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La línea base (baseline) son los datos tomados ANTES de la intervención. Sirven para comparar si el tratamiento realmente cambia la conducta."}, {"q": "A student walks up to the teacher and says \"may I go to the bathroom?\" What type of behavior is this?", "opts": ["A mand", "Polite", "An intraverbal", "Antecedent"], "ans": 0, "ex": "'¿Puedo ir al baño?' es un mand: una petición cuyo refuerzo es ir al baño. La conducta verbal pide acceso."}, {"q": "You just received a new client and are unsure how to run some of the programming. When should you consult with your BCBA?", "opts": ["Wait until your BCBA comes out and supervises you", "Before you get to your next session", "Don't worry about it, you will figure it out", "Change the program to something you understand better"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Ante una duda en la programación, consulta a tu BCBA EN CUANTO surja la duda (durante o antes de la sesión). No improvises ni cambies el programa."}, {"q": "At your most recent session the client's mom started to ask you about this new diet where youonly eat sunflower seeds. The mom said she read about it on the internet and saw a video claiming the diet could help cure autism. The mom asks for your opinion. What is the best course of action?", "opts": ["Tell her you don't have an opinion on the diet, and refer her to your supervisor", "Tell her how ridiculous she sounds", "Explain to her that you aren't familiar with that diet, but you know of other diets that could help", "Leave the case"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Nunca des tu opinión médica ni de nutrición: remite a la familia a tu BCBA/supervisor para hablar de dietas o tratamientos."}, {"q": "What is the best way to respond to feedback from your BCBA?", "opts": ["Engage in an arguement with your BCBA", "Talk about your BCBA behind their back", "Professionally. Use it to improve yourself, even if you don't agree with it", "Ignore it. What do they know?"], "ans": 2, "ex": "La mejor respuesta ante el feedback es ACEPTARLO, agradecerlo y aplicarlo, y preguntar de inmediato si hay dudas. Te ayuda a crecer profesionalmente."}, {"q": "What are the three components of good data?", "opts": ["True and verified", "IOA", "Confound", "Reliable, accurate, and valid"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Los tres componentes del buen dato: ser ACURADO, FIABLE y VÁLIDO. Sin precisión no sirve para decisiones."}, {"q": "What behavior is the most observable and measurable?", "opts": ["Your client fails a math test due to a lack of effort", "You fall asleep in class because you are tired", "You fall asleep in class", "Your client was stressed out and ate a big bag of cookies"], "ans": 2, "ex": "La conducta más observable y medible es la que se describe como una ACCIÓN contable y visible (frecuencia concreta), sin términos subjetivos."}, {"q": "What goes on the x-axis of a line graph?", "opts": ["Time", "Behavior", "Title", "Client name"], "ans": 0, "ex": "En el eje X (abscisa) va el TIEMPO o las sesiones (variable independiente). La conducta no va ahí."}, {"q": "What goes on the y-axis of a line graph", "opts": ["Time", "Behavior", "Title", "Client name"], "ans": 1, "ex": "En el eje Y (ordenada) va la medida de la conducta (frecuencia, duración, etc.), el nivel de la variable dependiente."}, {"q": "Your client elopes 5 times per hour. What does this describe?", "opts": ["Frequency", "IRT", "Rate", "Duration"], "ans": 2, "ex": "'Elopea 5 veces por hora' es una TASA (rate): frecuencia con componente de tiempo (por hora)."}, {"q": "You want to measure the time in between placing orders on amazon. What are you measuring?", "opts": ["Latency", "IRT", "Duration", "Rate"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El tiempo entre pedidos (entre respuestas) es IRT (tiempo entre respuestas). El tiempo desde la orden hasta el pedido sería latencia."}, {"q": "A client's mom reports to you that Abby tried 5 new foods since last session. What type of measurement is this?", "opts": ["IRT", "Duration", "Frequency", "Rate"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Que Abby probó 5 alimentos nuevos es un producto permanente/recuento del resultado: mides la consecuencia de la conducta (probó nuevos)."}, {"q": "If your client goes an entire week without calling his brother names, he earns a trip to game works. What reinforcement procedure is this?", "opts": ["DRA", "DRO", "SR-", "DRI"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Reforzar que pase la SEMANA completa sin la conducta es DRO: el refuerzo llega cuando la conducta problema ESTÁ AUSENTE."}, {"q": "Your client is going on a golf trip to August National and invites you to tag along. Are you allowed to go?", "opts": ["Yes, how could you pass that opportunity up?", "Yes, as long as you clear it with your supervisor", "No, this violates dual relationships and is unethical", "No, you aren't allowed to miss work"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Viajar por placer con el cliente crea una relación dual. No es permitido: se debe mantener la relación estrictamente profesional."}, {"q": "You and a client practice interview questions every session to prepare for his job interview. During the job interview he is able to answer every question and gets the job. What has your client demonstrated?", "opts": ["Maintenance", "Generilization", "Shaping", "Reinforcement"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Contestar en la entrevista REAL (otro ambiente) pese a practicar en sesión es generalización: la habilidad se usa en un contexto nuevo."}, {"q": "I want you to provide reinforcement every 5th response. What kind of schedule is this?", "opts": ["VR5", "FR5", "FR6", "VI1"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Reforzar CADA 5a respuesta es un programa de RAZÓN FIJA 5 (FR5): el número de respuestas es fijo."}, {"q": "When Tammy throws a tantrum, mom takes away her Barbie Dolls, and the tantrums decrease. What is happening?", "opts": ["Positive Reinforcement", "Negative Reinforcement", "Positive Punishment", "Negative Punishment"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Retirar las Barbies cuando hace berrinche (se quita algo) y el berrinche DISMINUYE = castigo negativo (remoción que reduce la conducta)."}, {"q": "It took me 2 hours to get home from work today due to traffic. I also stopped and picked up food on the way home, and went to the bank. What type of measurement did I use to measuremy car ride?", "opts": ["Duration", "Frequency", "IRT", "Rate"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Medias el viaje por el TIEMPO que te tomó (2 horas): es duración. Esa medida captura cuánto duró la conducta/evento."}, {"q": "At dinner, you make your Bumble date choose their favorite food: seafood or steak. What typeof preference assessment did you conduct?", "opts": ["Forced choice", "Multiple stimulus with replacement", "Multiple sitmulus without replacement", "Natural assessment"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Dar dos opciones (mariscos o filete) y que elija UNA es una evaluación de preferencia por elección pareada/forzada. Es la más directa para comparar dos items."}, {"q": "Your session lasts 3 hours, but your BCBA asks you take data on one specific behavior for only two 20 minute intervals per day. What type of measurement is this?", "opts": ["Continuous", "Discontinuous", "Duration", "Frequency"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Registrar la conducta SOLO en dos intervalos de 20 minutos dentro de la sesión es registro por intervalos (muestreo del tiempo), no una medida continua de toda la sesión."}, {"q": "It's nap time and I have 10 students in my class. Every 8 minutes I look up from my desk to see who isn't sleeping. What type of measurement?", "opts": ["Momentary time sampling", "Whole interval", "Partial interval", "Frequency"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Mirar cada 8 minutos si cada niño duerme es muestreo de tiempo MOMENTÁNEO (momentary time sampling): anotas lo que pasa justo en el instante."}, {"q": "Your daughter gets home from art class and you ask her if she learned anything. She shows you a beautiful painting of a house. What type of measurement are you using?", "opts": ["Duration", "IRT", "Permanent Product", "Latency"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El cuadro terminado es un producto permanente: la evidencia del trabajo de la niña. Mides el resultado de la conducta."}, {"q": "During session, your client falls and bumps their head. A knot forms and the client needs to see a doctor. What do you do?", "opts": ["Resign from your position", "Inform your BCBA and follow company protocols", "Try to hide the knot from the parents", "Nothing. It wasn't your fault"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Ante un golpe en la cabeza, primero la SEGURIDAD: informa y busca atención médica según protocolo y avisa a tu supervisor."}, {"q": "I'm teaching my client to count to 10. I start by teaching them to count to 3, and reinforcing. Then I reinforce only when they count to 7. Finally, I reinforce only when they get all the way to 10. What am I doing?", "opts": ["Chaining", "Shaping", "Measurement", "NET"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Exigir cada vez más aproximaciones (3 → 7 → 10) es modelado (shaping): refuerzas pasos cada vez más cercanos a la meta."}, {"q": "NET is the same as?", "opts": ["Naturalistic teaching", "DTT", "Table time", "Contrived teaching"], "ans": 0, "ex": "NET (Enseñanza en el Ambiente Natural) es igual a la enseñanza naturalista: aprender en situaciones cotidianas y funcionales."}, {"q": "While your supervisor is out of town, she asks you to conduct a functional analysis on your client. What should you do?", "opts": ["Do the functional analysis. You are well trained", "Report your BCBA to the board", "Quit your job", "Decline to do the functional analysis. You are not suited to do an FA alone as an RBT"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El RBT no conduce un análisis funcional solo: DECLINA y remite al BCBA. Realizar un FA exige entrenamiento y supervisión que no corresponde al RBT."}], "count": 100}, {"id": "exam3", "title": "Examen 3", "questions": [{"q": "Registered behavior technicians should be prepared to collect data. Which of the following answer choices is not part of preparing for data collection?", "opts": ["Read data from last session", "Determine what programs you will run", "Gather materials for programs", "Plan your programs after you arrive at the client's session"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Prepararse para la recolección de datos incluye repasar notas y tener materiales LISTOS antes de empezar. 'Planear el programa al llegar' NO forma parte de la preparación: se prepara de antemano."}, {"q": "There are advantages to permanent product recording. Which of the following answer choices best describes permanent product recording?", "opts": ["Dianne instructs her children to go clean their rooms before they leave for the day. 10 minutes later Dianne walks in the rooms to check and see if they are cleaning", "John set up cameras around the office so he could monitor work progress even when he was out of town or at his own home", "Mary was out sick on the day she was supposed to give a quiz. She asked the substitute to distribute the quiz anyway. The next day, Mary graded and scored the student's performance", "Glen tells his children to go upstairs and brush their teeth. When they come downstairs, Glen asks them if they are done brushing teeth"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El producto permanente mide el RESULTADO o efecto que deja la conducta después de ocurrir (objetos, trabajos, listas). No requiere registrar en vivo."}, {"q": "Your BCBA designs a new behavior plan to target your client's aggression. You implement it for two weeks, and then start to think that the plan isn't effective. What should you do?", "opts": ["Change the plan immediately. You shouldn't implement an ineffective plan", "Communicate with your BCBA immediately and share your thoughts with them", "Wait for further guidance from your BCBA before you do or say anything", "Start to train the parents on the plan. Part of the problem is the plan isn't being implemented at home"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Si en dos semanas crees que el plan no funciona, NO lo cambias por tu cuenta: mantén la fidelidad al plan y reporta tus preocupaciones a la BCBA, que decidirá ajustes."}, {"q": "Extinction, along with reinforcement and punishment, is a behavior change principle. Of the following answer choices, what does not accurately represent extinction?", "opts": ["Extinction works to reduce behavior", "Extinction works as a punishment procedure", "Extinction can involve planned ignoring", "Extinction should be implemented 100% of opportunities"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La extinción no es un castigo ni funciona como procedimiento de castigo. Es una afirmación que describe la extinción de forma INCORRECTA."}, {"q": "Bill and his mother in law do not get along. Bill's wife notices that whenever her mother plans a visit, Bill immediately books a golf outing with his friends. What would you hypothesize is the function of Bill's planning a golf trip behavior?", "opts": ["Attention", "Tangible", "Escape/Avoidance", "Automatic"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Bill planea el golf justo cuando la suegra va a visitar: la conducta evita/escapa de la situación aversiva. Función: escape/evitación."}, {"q": "Your best friend is an RBT. She works at the same company as you, and works under the supervision of the same BCBA. You like your BCBA, but your friend doesn't agree with the feedback that the BCBA gives. When the BCBA gives her feedback, she ignores it, and doesn't implement it or improve her services. What has your friend failed to do?", "opts": ["Actively seek clinical direction from a supervisor in a timely manner", "Respond appropriately to feedback", "Communicate with stakeholders", "Maintain professional boundaries to avoid dual relationships"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La amiga ignora y no implementa el feedback: fracasó en aceptar y RESPONDER al feedback para mejorar sus servicios. Eso viola el compromiso de supervisión."}, {"q": "Every 6 months Miranda receives her favorite bottle of wine from her boss as a thank you gift for her hard work throughout the year. The last two times Miranda received this gift, her siblings drank the entire bottle when they visited for the weekend. The next time her siblings visited her, Miranda hid the bottle and served other wine. What type of intervention did Miranda implement?", "opts": ["Antecedent", "Consequence", "Avoidance", "Differential reinforcement"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Ocultar el vino ANTES de la visita previene la conducta: es una intervención de ANTECEDENTE (modifica el ambiente antes de que ocurra el problema)."}, {"q": "You spent the first month with your client managing behaviors and identifying reinforcers. This week, your BCBA wants you to identify what your client can and can't do in terms of skills. What procedure are you most likely going to implement?", "opts": ["Task analysis procedures", "Probing procedures", "Generalization procedures", "Maintenance procedures"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Identificar qué sabe y qué no sabe el cliente (habilidades) es una EVALUACIÓN de habilidades (skills assessment). Es el paso previo a diseñar enseñanzas."}, {"q": "Mary's session notes included the following passage: \"When I arrived at session the client was eating breakfast. Mom asked him 3 times to pick up his trash and received no response. The fourth time she asked he screamed. The client was visibly frustrated at this point. I prompted the client to pick up his trash, and provided reinforcement upon completion.\" What should not be included in her session notes?", "opts": ["\"When I arrived at session the client was eating breakfast\"", "\"Mom asked him 3 times to pick up his trash and received no response\"", "\"The client was visibly frustrated at this point\"", "\"I prompted the client to pick up his trash, and provided reinforcement upon completion\""], "ans": 2, "ex": "'El cliente se veía visiblemente frustrado' es una INTERPRETACIÓN/juicio subjetivo. Las notas de sesión llevan solo hechos observables."}, {"q": "Your BCBA designs a token economy to use during discrete trial training. Your BCBA wants to target sitting in a chair, responding in a timely manner, and working promptly. Your BCBA instructs you to provide tokens every 3-5 correct responses. What answer choice accurately describes the reinforcement schedule you will be using?", "opts": ["FI4", "VI4", "FR4", "VR4"], "ans": 3, "ex": "'Fichas cada 3-5 respuestas correctas' (números variables) es un programa de RAZÓN VARIABLE (VR): el refuerzo llega según un promedio de respuestas."}, {"q": "You and your friends have a tradition where you set off hundreds of dollars of fireworks on the Fourth of July. Since you are preparing for your RBT exam, you want to measure one aspect of the fireworks. You are most interested in the length of time it takes to set off one firework after the last one went off. What would be the most appropriate measurement to use to track this?", "opts": ["Frequency", "Rate", "IRT", "Latency"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El tiempo entre un fuego artificial y el siguiente es IRT (tiempo entre respuestas): mides el intervalo que separa dos ocurrencias."}, {"q": "Jen’s husband golfs every Sunday morning with his buddies. Whenever he comes home he leaves his muddy shoes in the middle of the floor and Jen scolds him. Jen decides she will now give verbal attention to her husband when he puts his shoes in the closet, and will ignore him when he puts his shoes in the middle of the floor. What procedure is she using?", "opts": ["DRA", "DRI", "DRO", "DRL"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Atención por la conducta alternativa (zapatos en el clóset) y sin atención por la problemática = reforzamiento diferencial (DRA): refuerzas la alternativa."}, {"q": "RBTs have several roles in service delivery. Which of the following is NOT the role of an RBT", "opts": ["Implement behavior plans", "Conduct indirect assessments", "Assist with parent training", "Design reinforcement systems"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El RBT NO diseña intervenciones ni toma decisiones clínicas: su rol es implementar (aunque como conducta ética puede aportar ideas, la respuesta 'diseñar/basar el tratamiento' no es su rol)."}, {"q": "Ben is asked to assist his BCBA with a new client assessment. The two arrive at the client’s house and start to set-up. As they are setting up, the BCBA is asking the client “what’s your name?”, “what’s 2+2?”, “Can you spell dog?” What most likely explains what your BCBA is doing?", "opts": ["Probing", "Shaping", "Reinforcing", "Communication training"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Preguntar nombre, 2+2, deletrear 'dog'... el BCBA está tomando una evaluación inicial de habilidades (lo que el cliente sabe hacer)."}, {"q": "Yesterday, you were reviewing session notes from the past week. You start to notice that you and the other RBT on the team are running many of the skill acquisition programs differently. What is the most appropriate action to take in this scenario?", "opts": ["Call your BCBA and report the other RBT on the team for incorrectly running programs", "Ask your client’s parents how the other RBT does things and compare that to what you do", "Ignore it because it was only one week of data and notes", "Tell your BCBA and ask for clarification for yourself and the other RBT"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Si dos RBT implementan distinto, lo apropiado es pedir a la BCBA ACLARACIONES para el equipo completo, no inventar ni confrontar entre compañeros."}, {"q": "What measurement system in applied behavior analysis captures every instance that a behavior occurs?", "opts": ["Continuous measurement", "Discontinuous measurement", "Interval recording", "Permanent product recording"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Registrar CADA instancia de la conducta es una medición CONTINUA. Solo muestrean: intervalo parcial, completo y momentáneo."}, {"q": "Functional communication training is commonly used in ABA to teach clients how to communicate with those around them. During FCT you will reinforce successive approximations of desired communication. What is this called?", "opts": ["Probing", "Task analysis", "Shaping", "Receptive instruction"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Reforzar aproximaciones sucesivas a la comunicación deseada es MODELADO (shaping). El FCT se basa en reforzar acercamientos cada vez mejores."}, {"q": "Your client will occasionally scream at the top of their lungs. There are no clear antecedents or consequences. Your BCBA is attempting to figure out what the function of the behavior might be. Which of the following would NOT be the function of this behavior?", "opts": ["Attention", "Tangible", "Control", "Sensory"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Las cuatro funciones son atención, escape, tangible y automática. 'Control' NO es una función de la conducta."}, {"q": "RBTs are required to receive monthly supervision from a supervisor that is an approved provider of supervision. If you work 100 hours in April, what is the minimum amount of supervision hours you would need to meet requirements?", "opts": ["1 hour", "5 hours", "10 hours", "20 hours"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El RBT necesita supervisión del 5% de las horas. 5% de 100 horas = 5 horas. Es el mínimo mensual."}, {"q": "In which of the following scenarios would duration be the most appropriate measurement?", "opts": ["Your client has an eating disorder. You want to track the length of time in between meals to determine how often they are eating", "You are driving to the beach. You make a bet with a friend that your route is faster than theirs", "A teacher is tracking the number of attempts it takes for each group to solve 10 math problems correctly", "Your clients mom wants to reduce the amount of time it takes for your client to respond after she calls their name"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La duración es la mejor medida cuando lo importante es CUÁNTO TIEMPO dura la conducta (por ejemplo, tiempo en tarea o de llanto)."}, {"q": "Jim recorded the following description in his session notes: “I presented the workbook to the client. The client rolled out of his chair, and onto the floor. He put both of his hands over his ears, and screamed “no” What is Jim describing?", "opts": ["The function of the behavior", "The topography of the behavior", "The frequency of the behavior", "The magnitude of the behavior"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Jim describe lo que ocurre alrededor de la conducta: el antes, la conducta y lo que pasó (una descripción de la cadena A-B-C / topografía de la conducta)."}, {"q": "A skill acquisition plan contains several essential components. First, a skill must be identified. Then a goal is created to address the skill. Next, a measurement procedure is identified to use to record data. What is the next step in a skill acquisition plan?", "opts": ["Implement the procedures", "Collect and review intervention data", "Gather baseline data", "Modify the plan if necessary"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Después de identificar el objetivo y la medición, el siguiente paso del plan es elegir y aplicar el procedimiento de enseñanza (enseñar la habilidad)."}, {"q": "You are assisting your supervisor with parent training. During the training meeting, the parent mentions that getting ready for school is a constant struggle. Your BCBA recommends that the parent implement an intervention that allows the client to watch TV for 20 minutes in the morning if they get dressed and ready for school in a timely manner. Implementing this intervention establishes a __________?", "opts": ["Contingency", "Punisher", "Preference", "Function"], "ans": 0, "ex": "'Si se alista a tiempo, ve TV 20 minutos' es una CONTINGENCIA: relación si-entonces entre conducta y consecuencia."}, {"q": "Tommy will make noises with his mouth while sitting in math class. When Tommy makes noises, his teacher will tell him to quiet down. Tommy continues making noises. This week, the teacher decides she is no longer going to say anything to Tommy when he makes noises. Now, Tommy is making the noises louder and more frequently. Which of the following answer choices best describes this change in behavior?", "opts": ["Extinction", "Resistance to Extinction", "Extinction failure", "Extinction burst"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Cuando la maestra deja de atender los ruidos, Tommy los hace MÁS FUERTES y frecuentes: es un estallido de extinción (aumento temporal esperado)."}, {"q": "You just passed your RBT exam and are assigned your first case. Your client is a 13-year-old girl who engages in severe aggression towards others. Before you start the case, which of the following answer choices should be established?", "opts": ["DRO intervention", "Parent training", "Crisis/emergency plan", "Extinction procedures"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Antes de atender agresión severa se establece un PLAN de crisis/emergencia (y supervisión). La seguridad es la prioridad."}, {"q": "Last week, you decided to start a diet. You aren’t allowed to eat donuts at all during the week. On Saturdays, you allow yourself two hot and fresh Krispy Kreme donuts. Saturday morning you wake up and drive to Krispy Kreme. The “hot and fresh” sign is on, so you walk in and buy yourself two donuts. What is the SD for hot and fresh donuts in this scenario?", "opts": ["The diet", "It is Saturday morning", "The donut shop", "The hot and fresh sign"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El letrero 'hot and fresh' señala que los donuts están disponibles: es el estímulo discriminativo (SD) que hace probable entrar a comprar."}, {"q": "Understanding the function of a behavior is the first step to properly treating the behavior. Why is it crucial to understand the function of each behavior?", "opts": ["Function tells us what measurement system to use when tracking behavior", "Function tells us why the behavior is occurring", "Function tells us how often we should reinforce or punish a behavior", "Function tells us what the behavior looks like"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Entender la función es crucial porque el tratamiento debe basarse en ELLA: refuerzas una alternativa que cumpla la misma función de la conducta problema."}, {"q": "Fill in the blanks. Negative reinforcement involves ______ a stimulus which ______ behavior. Positive punishment involves _______ a stimulus which ______ behavior", "opts": ["adding; decreases; adding; increases", "removing; decreases; removing; increases", "removing; decreases; adding; increases", "removing; increases; adding; decreases"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Refuerzo negativo: RETIRAS un estímulo y AUMENTA la conducta. Castigo positivo: AGREGA un estímulo y DISMINUYE la conducta."}, {"q": "You are observing your client in a social setting on the weekends. Your BCBA asked you to record duration data for time spent talking to peers. For the first hour you recorded the following data: 5 minutes, 10 minutes, 8 minutes, 12 minutes. What percentage of the first hour did your client spend talking to peers?", "opts": ["50%", "54%", "58%", "41%"], "ans": 2, "ex": "(5+10+8+12) = 35 minutos de 60 = 58%. Divides los minutos de conducta entre el total de la hora."}, {"q": "Our clients are protected by privacy laws and ethical codes. In order to remain within the ethical standards laid out by the BACB, who should you talk to about specific details of your cases?", "opts": ["RBTs and BCBAs involved with the case", "Only RBTs involved with the case, and outside BCBAs not involved with the case", "RBTs that you work with that aren’t on the case, but know the client, and BCBAs involved with the case", "Only BCBAs involved with the case"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Los detalles del caso se comparten solo con el SUPERVISOR y el equipo involucrado en el caso. Todo lo demás viola la confidencialidad."}, {"q": "You spent the last month recording frequency data on how often your client insults their siblings. Your frequency data is broken down by the number of insults per session. You took data for a total of 10 sessions. If your BCBA asked you to graph this data, where would you record the frequency of insults data?", "opts": ["X-axis", "Y-axis", "Condition change line", "Graph legend"], "ans": 1, "ex": "En el gráfico de línea, la medida de la conducta (frecuencia de insultos) va en el eje Y. El tiempo/sesiones van en el eje X."}, {"q": "Your client is overweight and is seemingly only motivated by food. Your client requested that you no longer use food as a reinforcer. After talking with your BCBA, what might be the best course of action?", "opts": ["Continue using food reinforcers. It’s the only thing that works", "Pair the food with other unconditioned reinforcers to establish new reinforcers", "Refer the client to a dietician. ABA is not the right fit", "Immediately discontinue food reinforcers, and try new items until something works as a reinforcer"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Respetas la petición del cliente de no usar comida: buscas reforzadores alternativos que no pongan en riesgo su salud ni su dignidad."}, {"q": "Bobby works with a 19-year-old client who wants to learn to shop for his own groceries. The client is able to make a list and locate the items, but struggles using the self-checkout machines at the grocery store. The client is able to scan the items, place them in the bag, and run his credit card, but sometimes forgets what button to push before running the credit card, and how to complete the transaction. When Bobby works on this with his client, Bobby lets the client do the check-out process independently, and only teaches the steps the client doesn't know. What type of task chain teaching is this?", "opts": ["Forward chaining", "Backwards chaining", "Total task chaining", "Behavior chain interruption strategy"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El cliente completa TODA la cadena de forma independiente y tú solo enseñas los pasos que no domina: es encadenamiento por tarea total."}, {"q": "A new BCBA is assigned to a case that you have worked on for almost a year now. During the first supervision meeting, the new BCBA suggests you change how you are delivering reinforcement, and corrects the way you provide corrective feedback to your client. As an RBT, what is the most appropriate way you should respond in this situation?", "opts": ["Report the BCBA to your director or boss. Your BCBA should not be providing you feedback after only the first session", "Tell the BCBA you understand, but continue doing it your way when they leave", "Accept the feedback, and attempt to implement the changes. If you have questions about the changes, communicate immediately with the supervisor", "Explain to the BCBA that you respect their opinion, but the way you’re doing it has worked in the past, so you should continue doing it that way"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Ante el feedback del nuevo BCBA lo correcto es ACEPTARLO, implementarlo y preguntar de inmediato si hay dudas. No discutas ni ignores solo porque 'antes era distinto'."}, {"q": "Which of the following answer choices best describes behavior in observable and measurable terms?", "opts": ["Ryen kicked several students today at school. The kicking usually occurred as Ryen was changing classes. Ryen failed a test earlier in the day which led to the kicking", "Sydney pulled her sister’s hair during her session today. In response, her sibling pinched Sydney on the arm. Mom came upstairs and told both of them they could not have dessert", "Jimmy has been stressed out lately. He didn’t eat lunch, and when offered a snack he declined", "Susy had an episode today due to her bipolar diagnosis. In response, Susy’s mom scheduled a doctor’s appointment to up her medication"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Una conducta bien definida se describe en términos OBSERVABLES y MEDIBLES (acciones concretas y contables), sin estados internos."}, {"q": "Devin struggles starting and finishing games with peers. Your BCBA asked you to record data on peer play. It took Devin 6 minutes to start walking to the table when his peers asked him to play a game with them. Devin sat for 10 minutes, took 2 minutes in between turns, and then asked if he could be all done with the game 3 times. Which of the following answer choices represents the latency of Devin walking to the table?", "opts": ["6 minutes", "11 minutes", "5 minutes", "2 minutes"], "ans": 0, "ex": "La latencia es el tiempo desde el SD (que le pidan jugar) hasta el INICIO de la respuesta (empezar a caminar a la mesa) = 6 minutos."}, {"q": "Jim’s family goes out to eat quite often, but Jim is unable to order off the menu for himself. Viviana works with Jim at home on picking items on a menu, looking at prices, and communicating his selection to a waiter. The next time Jim goes to the restaurant, Jim orders a hamburger for himself. What did Jim exhibit at the restaurant?", "opts": ["Naturalistic Teaching", "Generalization", "Maintenance", "Differential reinforcement"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Jim ordena en el restaurante real (un entorno nuevo y natural): es GENERALIZACIÓN, usar lo aprendido en otro contexto."}, {"q": "Differential reinforcement is used to reduce behavior and teach skills in applied behavior analysis. Differential reinforcement can lead to ________?", "opts": ["Discrimination", "Differentiation", "Alternative behaviors", "All the above"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El reforzamiento diferencial enseña al cliente a DISCRIMINAR: la respuesta correcta recibe refuerzo y la otra no; surge una conducta más discriminada."}, {"q": "Punishment can be either socially mediated or automatic. Which of the following is the best example of automatic punishment?", "opts": ["You typically order the salmon roll from your local sushi place, but they are out of salmon. You order tuna instead", "Your little brothers are constantly fighting. Now, when they fight you take away their Xbox. They no longer fight when you are around", "You buy a brand new sweatshirt from a popular online store. When it arrives, you wear it for a day, but it is too tight and itchy. You no longer wear the sweatshirt", "It usually takes you 45 minutes to get to work. Today, you try a new route and turn down a different street. You get to work 20 minutes faster, and now always take that route"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Castigo AUTOMÁTICO: la consecuencia aversiva ocurre por sí misma, sin mediación social (como el suéter que pica y ya no se usa)."}, {"q": "Which of the following is true about stimulus preference assessments?", "opts": ["Stimulus preference assessments identify reinforcers for a client", "Stimulus preference assessments should be conducted indirectly", "Certain stimulus preference assessments can establish a hierarchy", "You should not run a stimulus preference assessment more than once a month"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Las evaluaciones de preferencia pueden ESTABLECER UNA JERARQUÍA: ordenar los artículos del más al menos preferido, útil para elegir reforzadores."}, {"q": "You work with a client four times a week for two hours each session. During your session, you take frequency data on your client’s screaming behavior. Last week, your client screamed 4 times during session 1, 8 times during session 2, 6 times during session 3, and 10 times during session 4. What was the rate of screaming per hour for session 3?", "opts": ["6 times per hour", "3 times per hour", "2 times per hour", "4 times per hour"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Razón 6 veces / 2 horas = 3 veces por hora. Divides el número de ocurrencias entre el tiempo de la sesión."}, {"q": "John is working on functions, features, and categories with his client. John taught his client that an apple fit into the fruit category. John’s client now says “fruit” when he sees an apple. John’s client also says “fruit” when he sees grapes, bananas, and pears. What is John’s client demonstrating?", "opts": ["Response generalization", "Stimulus generalization", "Maintenance", "Overgeneralization"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Responder 'fruit' a uvas, bananas y peras (estímulos parecidos) es generalización de ESTÍMULO: mismo operante ante estímulos semejantes."}, {"q": "Trash collection comes every Saturday in Sarah’s neighborhood. When Sarah’s husband leaves to play golf, he asks Sarah to put out the trash. Four hours later, Sarah hears the garbage truck coming down her street, so she rushes downstairs to put out the trash can. The sound of the garbage truck in relation to Sarah putting out the trash is a _______?", "opts": ["Motivating Operation", "Discriminative Stimuli", "Prompt", "Reinforcer"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El sonido del camión de basura marca el momento: es el estímulo discriminativo (SD) que pone la conducta de sacar la basura."}, {"q": "Your BCBA has an assessment scheduled for next Tuesday. She asks you to assist her with part of the assessment. She wants you to conduct the initial indirect assessment. Which of the following answer choices would be most appropriate as an indirect assessment?", "opts": ["Event recording", "Functional analysis", "Narrative recording", "Interview"], "ans": 3, "ex": "La evaluación INDIRECTA pregunta a otras personas (entrevistas, cuestionarios) en vez de observar directamente la conducta."}, {"q": "Bonnie will always grab a cookie right before dinner. This leads to her refusing to eat her dinner, and engaging in escape-maintained behavior to get away from the table. Your BCBA creates an intervention that involves Bonnie’s parents giving Bonnie two cookies after dinner if Bonnie does not eat a cookie before dinner. What type of intervention is this?", "opts": ["Differential reinforcement of alternative behaviors", "Differential reinforcement of other behaviors", "Generalization training", "Punishment"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Dar dos galletas DESPUÉS de la cena si Bonnie NO come galleta antes: refuerzas la AUSENCIA de la conducta = DRO."}, {"q": "As an RBT, you are required to be prepared for a session as described by the skill acquisition plan. Which of the following is NOT one way you should prepare for your session?", "opts": ["Before you arrive for session, make sure you have all the materials you may need to implement the treatment plan", "Discuss any changes with the other RBTs and supervisors on the team after each of your sessions", "Communicate with your supervisor immediately when you are unsure of how to implement an intervention", "Once you arrive at your session, review all notes from prior sessions, and plan out your day"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Prepararse incluye revisar notas y material ANTES de la sesión. 'Planear los programas al llegar' no es una forma correcta de prepararse."}, {"q": "Chris is allowed to stay at home by himself during summer vacation while his mom is at work. When his mom leaves in the morning, she gives Chris a list of items that she needs him to complete. What would be the best way for Chris’ mom to measure whether or not Chris completed the entire list?", "opts": ["Direct assessment", "Event recording", "Permanent product recording", "Ask Chris when she got home"], "ans": 2, "ex": "La mejor forma de medir si hizo la lista completa es el PRODUCTO PERMANENTE: revisar los resultados/la lista terminada."}, {"q": "Jake is a 12-year-old boy who lives at home with his dad. Jake will often interrupt his dad’s work calls at inappropriate times. It was determined that the function of this behavior was attention from Jake’s dad. Your BCBA instructs you to give Jake attention every 3 minutes continuously while Jake’s dad is on a work call. What type of intervention does this most likely represent?", "opts": ["Non-contingent Reinforcement (NCR)", "Punishment", "VI3", "FR3"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Dar atención cada 3 minutos CONTINUAMENTE (sin requerir conducta) es reforzamiento NO contingente (NCR): se da el reforzador de forma programada."}, {"q": "While conducting forced-choice preference assessments, you start to notice that your client always chooses the item on the right-hand side. If you wanted to avoid this, which of the following answer choices would be most appropriate?", "opts": ["Continue running the forced-choice assessment, but prompt the client to occasionally choose from the left side", "Switch to a single-stimulus preference assessment", "Conduct a multiple-stimulus preference assessment instead", "Select reinforcers for your client without running a preference assessment"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Para evitar el sesgo al lado derecho, ALTERNAR/ALEATORIZAR la posición de los estímulos en cada ensayo."}, {"q": "Your client engages in a repetitive behavior that looks like pinching his own arm. This has started to cause minor irritation to your client’s skin. Your BCBA asks you to take partial interval data on your client’s pinching. You are taking data across 6 30-second intervals. The following data was recorded for each interval: 1 instance, 8 instances, 0 instances, 5 instances, 9 instances, 11 instances. Using partial interval recording, how many responses would you record?", "opts": ["5", "6", "34", "0"], "ans": 0, "ex": "En intervalo parcial, SI la conducta ocurre en CUALQUIER momento del intervalo se marca. Ocurrió en 5 de los 6 intervalos (solo el 3° fue 0)."}, {"q": "Money, tokens, and praise are all examples of what type of reinforcement?", "opts": ["Positive", "Primary", "Secondary", "Unconditioned"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Dinero, fichas y elogios son reforzadores CONDICIONADOS: su valor se aprende al asociarse con otros reforzadores."}, {"q": "Ben wanted to learn how to order his own meal at the local sushi restaurant. You worked with Ben on ordering a California roll from the menu on his own. Once Ben learned how to order the California roll, Ben started ordering chicken teriyaki, salmon rolls, and spicy tuna rolls from the menu. Ben’s ordering is an example of __________?", "opts": ["Stimulus Generalization", "Response Generalization", "Maintenance", "Tacting"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Ben aprende a pedir un 'California roll' y también pide otros platillos nuevos: VARIAS respuestas nuevas a estímulos parecidos = generalización de RESPUESTA."}, {"q": "Jennifer has four children. She cooks them all breakfast each morning. Jennifer’s 5-year-old son, who you work with in the morning, will throw his food at the other siblings while at the breakfast table. After an assessment, your BCBA determined that the food throwing was maintained by attention. Your BCBA instructed you to praise your client, and provide him with attention, every 2 minutes that he doesn’t throw food. What type of intervention are you implementing?", "opts": ["DRI", "DRA", "DRO", "DRL"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Elogiarlo/atenderlo cada 2 minutos en que NO tira comida es DRO: refuerzas la ausencia de la conducta objetivo."}, {"q": "Micah is generally well-behaved, but prefers staying up late with his family. Whenever Micah’s mom says “time to get ready for bed,” Micah will start to cry, and beg to stay up late. What function most likely describes Micah’s response to mom saying “time to get ready for bed?”", "opts": ["Escape/Avoidance", "Attention", "Access to a tangible", "Automatic"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Micah llora y suplica para EVITAR acostarse: la conducta le evita la demanda (escape/evitación)."}, {"q": "Glen is running DTT with his client. Glen provides the SD, waits for a response from the learner, provides a prompt to the learner, provides feedback, and then pauses briefly before providing the next SD. What did Glen do wrong?", "opts": ["Paused before the next SD", "Provided feedback after the response", "Waited for a response from the learner", "Provided the prompt after the response"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Glen entregó la ayuda DESPUÉS de la respuesta: el prompt debe ir ANTES (o durante) para asegurar la respuesta correcta. Es lo que hizo mal."}, {"q": "You are teaching your client how to boil noodles for spaghetti. You prompt then to take out the pot, fill it with water, put it on the stove, turn the stove on, wait for the water to boil, put the noodles in, check the noodles to see if they are ready, and then you provide them praise as reinforcement for draining the noodles when done. What type of task chaining are you implementing?", "opts": ["Forward", "Backward", "Total task", "Interruption strategy"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Enseñar TODA la cadena (olla → agua → estufa → ... → escurrir) con refuerzo al final es encadenamiento por TAREA TOTAL: todos los pasos juntos."}, {"q": "Jen works with a 6-year-old client three times a week. Whenever she is at the client’s house, she will talk about the Las Vegas Golden Knights with her client’s parents. Her client’s parents know how much Jen likes the Knights, so they buy her a jersey the next time they go to the game. If Jen accepts the jersey, this would most likely represent a _____?", "opts": ["Conflict of interest", "Lack of communication", "Acceptable scenario", "Illegal activity"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Aceptar la camiseta (obsequio de los padres del cliente) crea una relación dual/conflicto de interés. Debe declinarse."}, {"q": "Which of the following best represents an example of discontinuous measurement?", "opts": ["During recess, you record how many times your client engages with other student", "While at home, you record how long it takes for your son to complete his homework each night", "During a 2-hour movie you take data for 15 minutes on your client’s attending", "You record how many times your client elopes during your 3 hour sessions"], "ans": 2, "ex": "La medición discontinua MUESTREA la conducta: registro de intervalo parcial/completo y muestreo momentáneo. Solo estos son discontinuos."}, {"q": "Susie loves to draw with her sister after school. However, Susie’s sister will sometimes try to draw on Susie’s paper. Whenever Susie’s sister tries to draw on Susie’s paper, Susie will get up from the table and tell her “I am done drawing with you.” Susie’s sister is now drawing on Susie’s paper less than before. Susie getting up the table and telling her sister she isn’t going to draw with her is an example of _____________?", "opts": ["Positive reinforcement", "Negative reinforcement", "Positive punishment", "Negative punishment"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Susie se levanta y se va (QUITA la interacción/atención) y el comportamiento de la hermana DISMINUYE: remoción que reduce la conducta = castigo negativo."}, {"q": "You are watching the Olympics and keeping track of how many medals the USA has won. Counting the medals is an example of what type of measurement?", "opts": ["Frequency", "Partial interval recording", "IRT", "Duration"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Contar medallas es FRECUENCIA: registras cada instancia (cada medalla) y sumas."}, {"q": "You share a room with another RBT at the clinic where you work. The RBT asks you to discreetly take data on their client for 10 minutes to reduce reactivity. Every 60 seconds, you look up and check to see if the client is engaging in the target behavior. If the client is engaging in the target behavior, you mark it down as a response. What type of measurement are you implementing?", "opts": ["Frequency", "Momentary time sampling", "Partial interval recording", "Continuous measurement"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Revisar cada 60 segundos SI está ocurriendo la conducta es muestreo de tiempo MOMENTÁNEO (momentary time sampling)."}, {"q": "John’s parents really want him to enroll in school next year, but they are also considering homeschooling him for the first year or two. During your session, John’s mom starts to ask you several questions about schooling and what you think they should do. What is the best response to John’s mom’s questions?", "opts": ["Give her your honest opinion on schooling", "Ignore her requests, and change the subject", "Recommend that she consults with your supervisor, and decline to give your opinion", "Ask to come off the case. This is a conflict of interest"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Sobre decisiones de escolaridad NO respondes a nivel personal: refieres a la familia a tu SUPERVISOR/BCBA, que es quien orienta en estos casos."}, {"q": "If you were to demonstrate a shaping procedure to a new RBT who asked for your help, what would the procedure look like?", "opts": ["Present a cookie to your client. Give them the cookie only when they say “cookie.”", "Provide your client with tokens for target behaviors. When your client reaches 6 tokens, have them exchange the tokens for a cookie", "Put a box of cookies where your client can see them. Hold out a note card that has “cookie, please” written on it. Gradually fade out the words, and the note card", "Give your client a cookie whenever they make the “c” sound. As you progress, only give the cookie when the client’s verbal attempts come closer to saying “cookie.”"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El modelado (shaping) refuerza aproximaciones sucesivas hacia la meta, empezando por lo que el cliente ya hace y acercándolo al objetivo."}, {"q": "Grace provides her client a break when she earns 5 tokens. Grace also provides her client with two bonus tokens before DTT starts. The bonus tokens represent extra minutes on break. Grace utilizes a FR3 schedule and a response cost. What type of procedure is a response cost?", "opts": ["Positive punishment", "Negative punishment", "Time-out", "Reprimand"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El costo de respuesta es un CASTIGO: QUITAR fichas/reforzadores al ocurrir la conducta, lo que la DISMINUYE. Las fichas de bonificación son otro tema."}, {"q": "Your BCBA requested that you film a portion of your session for her to see. You comply, and film 10 minutes of session using your iPhone. Later on, while at dinner with your friends, you are showing your friends pictures on your iPhone and the video starts to play. Your client is clearly visible in the video. Have you maintained client dignity in this scenario?", "opts": ["Yes, you didn’t give out any personal information about the client. Your friends do not know anything about the client", "Yes, your BCBA gave you permission to film the client", "No, you violated the client’s privacy", "No, you should never film a client even when instructed to by a supervisor"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Enseñar a amigos un video donde el cliente aparece claramente ROMPE la dignidad y confidencialidad del cliente. No es apropiado."}, {"q": "Which of the following answer choices best represents discrimination training?", "opts": ["Your client wants to go on a diet. You work with them on identifying and ordering healthy and unhealthy foods at a restaurant", "You provide your client with Dr. Pepper only when they answer five questions in a row without protest", "When your client screams, you ignore the behavior, and focus your attention on something else", "During your client’s break, you will leave out water and snacks in an attempt to evoke spontaneous communication from your client"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Entrenamiento en discriminación: ante un estímulo hay refuerzo y ante otro no; el cliente aprende a responder de forma distinta a cada uno."}, {"q": "RBTs are expected to stay in good standing with the BACB. This includes renewing their RBT license as required. Part of the renewal process is retaking the competency assessment. How often do RBTs need to retake the competency assessment?", "opts": ["Every 6 months", "Every year", "Every 5 years", "As needed"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El RBT renueva su competencia (competency assessment) CADA AÑO para mantenerse en buen estado con el BACB."}, {"q": "Dan is working in a group home for adults. One of the residents of the group home wants to quit smoking. Dan gets together with his BCBA and they design a couple of different treatment options. One treatment option does not utilize punishment, while one does. The client wants to use the treatment option that uses punishment because they believe it will be more effective. What is the best course of action to take?", "opts": ["Use the punishment procedure, but be sure to include a reinforcement component as well", "Use the punishment procedure by itself without any reinforcement component", "Deny the client’s request. You should not use punishment when other options are available", "Deny the client’s request. They do not have a say in treatment decisions"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Estando disponible una opción basada en refuerzo, se elige la intervención que NO usa castigo: el castigo se evita cuando hay alternativas."}, {"q": "Another name for the y-axis on a line graph is the _________?", "opts": ["Abscissa", "Ordinate", "Baseline", "Trend Line"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El eje Y en un gráfico de línea se llama ORDENADA (ordinate). El eje X es la abscisa."}, {"q": "RBTs are a major part of the service delivery team in ABA. What is the RBTs primary role in service delivery?", "opts": ["Parent Training", "Behavior Management", "Implementation", "Functional Communication Training"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El papel principal del RBT en el equipo es la IMPLEMENTACIÓN (aplicar los programas directamente con el cliente)."}, {"q": "You are given a bag of items to bring to your client’s home on your first day of service. The bag contains a variety of stimuli that is age appropriate for your client. If you wanted to conduct a preference assessment using all the stimuli at once, what method would be most appropriate?", "opts": ["Single stimulus assessment", "Forced choice assessment", "Multiple stimulus assessment", "Reinforcer assessment"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Presentar TODOS los estímulos a la vez para que el cliente elija es una evaluación de estímulo PARCIAL/MÚLTIPLE (multiple stimulus)."}, {"q": "Dave is using a token economy to reinforce his client as his client completes math problems. Dave delivers a token every couple of problems that his client completes independently. What best describes this type of reinforcement?", "opts": ["Continuous", "Intermittent", "Natural", "Non-contingent"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Ficha 'cada un par de problemas' (sin número fijo) es un programa de RAZÓN VARIABLE (VR)."}, {"q": "As an RBT, you will be involved in task analysis and behavior chains. What is the distinction between the two?", "opts": ["There is no distinction", "Task analysis are forward chains, and behavior chains are backward chains", "Task analysis breaks down complex behavior. You teach the behavior chain", "The two are unrelated"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El análisis de tarea DESCOMPONE la conducta compleja en pasos; el encadenamiento enseña y une esos pasos en secuencia."}, {"q": "Tina is a 4th grader in a general education classroom. Two months ago, Tina would get up from her seat several times during class for attention. A behavior plan that utilized extinction was put in place, and the behavior went away. Last week, Tina got up from her seat 10 times in one class. What is the most likely explanation for the behavior occurring again?", "opts": ["Extinction burst", "Spontaneous Recovery", "Tina is automatically reinforced", "Tina is bored in class"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La reaparición temporal de una conducta extinta es RECUPERACIÓN ESPONTÁNEA: no significa que el plan falló, solo hay que seguir siendo consistente."}, {"q": "If you are working with a client, and accidentally reinforce a behavior, what is the best course of action for you to take as an RBT?", "opts": ["Let the parents know immediately", "Let your supervisor know as soon as possible", "Don’t report it, but make sure you correct your mistake", "Overcorrect your mistake by punishing the reinforced behavior"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Si reforzaste por error, no lo ocultes: REGISTRA y reporta a la BCBA. La transparencia mantiene la fidelidad del plan."}, {"q": "Reinforcement and punishment are both acceptable interventions, but reinforcement should always be used whenever possible instead of punishment. Which of the following answer choices describes a potential problem with punishment?", "opts": ["Punishment is not permanent. If you stop punishment, the behavior will come back", "Punishment does not reach a replacement behavior", "Clients can resist punishment, leading to harsher forms of punishment", "All the above"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Un problema del castigo: produce efectos secundarios (agresividad, evitación, daño a la relación) y NO enseña una conducta alternativa."}, {"q": "Brynn is working on functional communication with her daughter. She wants her daughter to make requests appropriately. Brynn will play a song that she knows her daughter does not like. Only when Brynn’s daughter says “please stop playing this song” will Brynna stop playing the song. Stopping the song is ____________?", "opts": ["Positive Reinforcement", "Negative Reinforcement", "Positive Punishment", "Negative Punishment"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Detener la canción cuando la hija PIDE (SE QUITA un estímulo aversivo y aumenta el pedido) es REFORZAMIENTO NEGATIVO."}, {"q": "The last three sessions your client’s dad reported to you that the client is going to bed at midnight and waking up at 4am. What course of action should you take as the RBT?", "opts": ["Report this to your BCBA, and make a note in your session notes", "Offer advice to the dad on sleeping techniques", "Modify your treatment on the days that your client did not sleep well", "Allow your client to take a nap if they request to do so during session"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Reportar los horarios extremos de sueño a tu BCBA es lo correcto: el RBT informa y el supervisor decide el curso de acción."}, {"q": "Use the graph below. What is the average frequency of elopement for Chad per session?", "opts": ["6", "4", "5", "25"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El promedio de frecuencia de escapadas (fugas) por sesión según el gráfico es 5. Se suma el total y se divide entre las sesiones."}, {"q": "AJ is a non-verbal 5-year-old who receives services in a clinical setting. AJ’s team uses errorless teaching with him when working on receptive color identification, and matching. AJ will now wait for a physical prompt before selecting a color when given an SD. What best describes AJ he relates to prompting?", "opts": ["AJ is resistant to prompts", "AJ is prompt dependent", "AJ is manipulating the RBTs", "AJ is too old to receive physical prompts"], "ans": 1, "ex": "AJ espera la ayuda física para responder: es DEPENDENCIA DE AYUDA (prompt dependence). El objetivo de las ayudas es transferir el control a los estímulos naturales."}], "count": 80}, {"id": "practice2", "title": "Examen de Práctica 2", "questions": [{"q": "Which of the following is the best example of maintaining client dignity?", "opts": ["Explaining to the waitress that your client has autism during a CBI", "Not restricting the client's right to food or water", "Sharing a client's information with a peer", "Sharing a client's private information with other RBTs"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Mantener la dignidad es NO RESTRINGIR derechos básicos del cliente (comer, beber, privacidad). Consta en el compromiso ético de respeto."}, {"q": "As an RBT you are required to know why behavior happens. These are commonly referred to as functions of behavior. What are the four functions?", "opts": ["escape, tangible, automatic, attention", "escape, sadness, control, tangible", "sensory, automatic, tangible, escape", "attention, fear, anger, tangible"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Las cuatro funciones: ESCAPE (evitar demandas), TANGIBLE (acceso a objetos), AUTOMÁTICA (sensorial) y ATENCIÓN. Es la base de todo análisis funcional."}, {"q": "When you answer questions in science class you receive praise, so you continue answering questions. When you answer questions during English class, you receive no praise, and stop answering questions. What is this an example of?", "opts": ["shaping", "differential reinforcement", "punishment", "positive reinforcement"], "ans": 1, "ex": "En ciencias la conducta recibe refuerzo y en inglés no: el cliente DISCRIMINA cuándo la respuesta funciona. Es discriminación de estímulos."}, {"q": "Which of the following is part of an RBT's role during service delivery?", "opts": ["Babysitting for the client", "Implement the skill acquisition plan", "Conducting FBAs", "Modifying the treatment plan"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El rol del RBT durante la prestación de servicios es la IMPLEMENTACIÓN directa de los programas bajo supervisión del BCBA."}, {"q": "As your friend is leaving your house, you notice they left their phone on the counter. You yell to your friend \"wait!\" causing your friend to turn around. Seein the phone is a?", "opts": ["MO", "Consequence", "SD", "Behavior"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El teléfono en el mostrador es el estímulo discriminativo (SD): su presencia señala que la respuesta de recuperarlo/reclamarlo funcionará."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an example of extinction?", "opts": ["Your client spent $30 a day on Roblox last month. His parents found out, and removed the credit card from his account. Now when he attempts to spend money on Roblox, he isn't able to buy anything", "Anytime you cut yourself, you apply a band aid to stop the bleeding", "During allergy season you are constantly sneezing and sniffling. Every day during allergy season, you take medicine to stop the sneezing", "At an Italian restaurant you order chicken parmesan. The waiter brings you spaghetti and meatballs. You request to talk to the manager and the manager apologizes and brings you your correct meal"], "ans": 0, "ex": "La extinción consiste en RETIRAR el refuerzo que mantenía la conducta para que deje de ocurrir. Sin identificación del refuerzo no funciona."}, {"q": "You have worked with a client for 6 months now and have a good relationship with the family. The mom needs a babysitter and asks your BCBA if you can take the job. The BCBA says of course and directs you to babysit Saturday night for the family. What should you do?", "opts": ["Tell them you will babysit but cancel at the last minute to protect yourself", "Babysit for the family. You must listen to your supervisor", "Request to come off the case. Your relationship with the family is now too personal", "Decline and remind your BCBA that babysitting the client without the parents home and off the clock would be unethical"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Cuidar al cliente como niñera fuera del horario crea una relación dual. DECLINA y recuerda que hacerlo fuera del ámbito profesional no es ético, incluso si un supervisor lo pide."}, {"q": "Which of the following best describes behavior?", "opts": ["Bill doesn't like being hot, so he turns on the air conditioner", "Susan dropped her pencil, and then turned on the light", "Tim is scared of the dark, so he turns on all the lights", "Greg is tired, so he turned off the lights"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La conducta es TODO lo que una persona HACE que es OBSERVABLE y MEDIBLE. Los estados internos no son conducta."}, {"q": "Your client is a 3 year old girl with autism. Throughout the day she will stick coins in her mouth. Whenever you tell her to stop she smiles and continues to do it. Although she hasn't swallowed the coins, it is possible she could someday. What would be the best and quickest intervention for this behavior?", "opts": ["Put the behavior on extinction. Attention appears to be reinforcing the client putting coins in their mouth and the client hasn't swallowed coins before", "Send your client to time out every time they put coins in their mouth", "Continue to tell your client how dangerous it is to put coins in their mouth. They need to learn safety skills", "Hide all available coins and block your client from accessing coins"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Riesgo de seguridad inmediato: RETIRAR/OCULTAR las monedas y bloquear el acceso. Ante un peligro de atragantamiento, la seguridad va primero."}, {"q": "Which of the following is the last step in a skill acquisition plan?", "opts": ["Modify the plan if necessary", "Implement the plan", "Identify a goal", "Collect and analyze skill data"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El último paso del plan de adquisición de habilidades es AJUSTARLO según los datos cuando sea necesario. Primero vienen meta, medición, implementación y recolección de datos."}, {"q": "A ___ signals that reinforcement is available", "opts": ["SDelta", "SD", "MO", "SP"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El SD señaliza que el REFUERZO está disponible. El EO/MO altera el valor del refuerzo, y el SΔ señala que NO estará disponible."}, {"q": "You are upstairs killing time while you cook your frozen pizza in the over. 18 minutes later you hear the oven go off. It takes you 10 seconds to start walking to the oven. The 10 seconds represents what?", "opts": ["Duration", "IRT", "Latency", "Rate"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Los 10 segundos entre el pitido del horno y empezar a caminar son LATENCIA: tiempo desde el SD hasta el inicio de la respuesta."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an abscissa?", "opts": ["x-axis", "phase change line", "y-axis", "baseline"], "ans": 0, "ex": "La abscisa es el eje X (tiempo/sesiones). La ordenada es el eje Y (la conducta)."}, {"q": "All of the following are appropriate for conducting a task analysis EXCEPT", "opts": ["Observe a competent individual perform the task", "Observe someone that is of equal skill in relation to your client", "Perform the task yourself", "Consult with experts or skilled persons performing the task"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Para un análisis de tarea observas a una persona COMPETENTE o expertos. Observar a alguien del mismo nivel que tu cliente NO sirve para aprender los pasos correctos."}, {"q": "You are starting a brand new client tomorrow. Your BCBA asks you to collect data on matching skills and imitation skills before intervention starts. What type of data are you collecting?", "opts": ["DRO", "Inaccurate", "Baseline", "Continuous"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Datos de habilidades ANTES de intervenir = datos de LÍNEA BASE. Sirven para comparar el efecto del programa después."}, {"q": "The goal of a stimulus preference assessment is what?", "opts": ["Determine what skills your client wants to work on", "Identify reinforcers", "Identify possible motivators", "Determine treatment goals"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El objetivo de la evaluación de preferencias es IDENTIFICAR posibles reforzadores/motivadores del cliente para usarlos en la enseñanza."}, {"q": "Consequences affect ____ behavior?", "opts": ["current", "current and future", "future", "past"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Las consecuencias afectan el comportamiento FUTURO (su probabilidad aumenta o disminuye) e incluso el actual, pero el efecto central es sobre el futuro."}, {"q": "Tom has been learning how to swing a golf club in his backyard using plastic balls and a net. Tomorrow he is going to go play a round of golf on a real course. If Tom is able to competently swing his clubs on the course, he would be doing what?", "opts": ["Shaping", "Generalizing", "Maintenance", "Reinforcing"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Practicar en el patio y responder bien en el campo real es GENERALIZACIÓN: la habilidad funciona en un contexto nuevo."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an example of a dual relationship?", "opts": ["You attend your client's birthday party as a friend and not a technician", "Taking your client to a restaurant as part of a interventions with the approval of your CBI", "You work with a client in school and in home", "Each session the parent spends an hour with you observing"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Asistir a la fiesta de cumpleaños del cliente como AMIGO crea una relación dual entre tu vida personal y la profesional."}, {"q": "Which of the following would be an inappropriate way to identify preferences for your client?", "opts": ["Ask their parents what the client likes", "Find a top 10 list of things children like on the internet", "Ask the client what they like", "Observe the client in their natural environment"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Identificar preferencias 'por Internet' (listas genéricas de lo que a los niños les gusta) NO es apropiado: las preferencias se evalúan con el cliente real."}, {"q": "You are told to observe mouthing behavior by your client. You record the first instance of mouthing after 10 minutes, the second instance after 15 minutes, and the third instance after 30 minutes. What is the average interreponse time?", "opts": ["12 minutes", "15 minutes", "10 minutes", "30 minutes"], "ans": 2, "ex": "IRT promedio: tiempo entre respuestas (2° instancia 5 min después de la 1ª; 3ª, 15 min después). (5+15)/2 = 10 minutos."}, {"q": "What occurs right before the behavior?", "opts": ["antecedent", "consequence", "motivating operation", "behavior"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El ANTECEDENTE es lo que ocurre justo antes de la conducta y hace probable que ocurra."}, {"q": "You are working with a client in-home and suspect abuse is occurring. What should you do?", "opts": ["Report it to your supervisor and the appropriate authorities. You are a mandated reporter", "Nothing. It isn't your business", "Report it just to your BCBA and let them handle it", "Call the police immediately"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Ante sospecha de abuso, REPORTA a tu supervisor y a las autoridades correspondientes: el RBT es reportante obligatorio."}, {"q": "Which of the following would be the best way to fade reinforcement from thickest schedule to thinnest schedule?", "opts": ["FR -> VI -> Fi", "FI -> FR -> VR", "VI -> FI -> FR", "FR -> FI -> VR"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Para desvanecer el refuerzo de lo más denso a lo más fino: FR (continuo) → FI → VR. Esta secuencia reduce el refuerzo sin perder la conducta."}, {"q": "You are trying to gain compliance with your client. You decide to give them 3 easy requests in a row, and then follow it up with a harder task. What are you trying to do?", "opts": ["Prompt the behavior", "Gain behavior momentum", "Shape the behavior", "Reinforce the behavior"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Dar varias peticiones fáciles antes de una difícil crea MOMENTUM conductual (inercia de cumplimiento): la persona se mantiene respondiendo."}, {"q": "You are working with a client in an adult group home. Your client is a heavy drinker who wants to quit drinking. With your help, your BCBA develops a behavior contract stating that your client will not have more than three drinks per week for the next month. Your client upholds his end of the contract for the first two weeks, then on the third week your client expresses he wants out of the behavior contract, and is going to have four drinks that night. What should you do?", "opts": ["Report your client to your supervisor and terminate services", "Recommend to the client they continue with the contract, but it is ultimately their choice", "Check your client into a rehab facility", "Prevent your client from drinking. They are not allowed to per the contract"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El cliente decide salirse del contrato. Lo correcto es respetar su autonomía recomendándole seguir, PERO la decisión final es del cliente."}, {"q": "All of the following are examples of continuous measurement except ___?", "opts": ["latency", "IRT", "interval recording", "duration"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Medidas continuas: frecuencia, duración, latencia, IRT. El registro de intervalo NO es continuo: muestrea el tiempo."}, {"q": "You say \"1, 2\" and your client says \"3.\" You then say \"old mcdonald had a\" and your client says \"farm.\" What are you working on?", "opts": ["Echoics", "Tacts", "Intraverbals", "Mands"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Completar '1,2'→'3' y 'old mcdonald had a'→'farm' son INTRAVERBALES: responder con palabras a otras palabras."}, {"q": "You’re about to start a session with a client. What do you need to do to be sure you’re ready to have a successful session (at the very minimum)?", "opts": ["Text your BCBA before every session to ask what you should run", "You should conduct a functional behavioral assessment and a preference assessment", "Read the session notes from the previous session", "Show up to every session with new potential reinforcers"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Como mínimo, LEER las notas de la sesión anterior (y revisar programas/materiales) para retomar el caso correctamente."}, {"q": "Data collected should be all of the following EXCEPT ____?", "opts": ["Valid", "Reliable", "Approved", "Accurate"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Los datos deben ser VÁLIDOS, ACURADOS y FIABLES. 'Aprobado' no es una propiedad de los datos: esa es la excepción."}, {"q": "You are working on gaining stimulus control over your client. Your client will sometimes flip over his chair when presented with a demand. Today, your client flipped over their chair. You asked them to pick it up, they complied, and you started clapping. Now, your client will no longer pick up their chair when you ask. Clapping acted as _____?", "opts": ["Positive punishment", "Positive reinforcement", "Negative punishment", "Negative reinforcement"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Aplaudir (se AGREGA algo) y el comportamiento de levantar la silla DISMINUYE: es castigo positivo."}, {"q": "Which of the following is NOT an example of a prompt?", "opts": ["Before you start cooking you put all the ingredients you need on the counter so you include everything that the recipe calls for", "When you ask your client want 2+2 is, you give them marbles to count. Your client answers \"2+2 = 6\"", "You're training discrimination with a client. You say \"point to triangle\" and then you look at triangle. Your client points to triangle", "You leave $10 on the counter to remind your partner to pick up coffee on their way home"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Darle bolitas para contar cuando respondes 2+2 no es una ayuda para esa respuesta: es manipular el ambiente, no guiar la respuesta correcta (eso no es un prompt)."}, {"q": "A motivating operation _____ and an SD _____?", "opts": ["comes after an SD, comes after a prompt", "alters the value of a reinforcer, signals a reinforcer is available", "signals a reinforcer is available, alters the value of a reinforcer", "comes before the SD, comes after the prompt"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El EO/MO altera el VALOR del reforzador; el SD señala la DISPONIBILIDAD del refuerzo. Cambian cosas distintas."}, {"q": "Tiffany is mand training with her client Bella. When Bella asks for water or apples, she should receive water or apples. When Bella asks her mom for water, she is immediately given water. When Bella asks her brother for water, her brother will often ignore her. Bella now only asks her mom for water, and not her brother. What is this considered?", "opts": ["stimulus generalization", "stimulus discrimination", "response generalization", "response discrimination"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Bella pide solo a quien SÍ responde (mamá) y no al que la ignora (hermano): aprende a DISCRIMINAR estímulos/personas."}, {"q": "Before you implement an extinction procedure, what ethical responsibility do you have?", "opts": ["Consult with your local authorities", "Inform the caregivers and those around the client that an extinction burst may occur", "There are not ethical considerations for extinction", "Consult with legal representatives"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Éticamente, antes de la extinción se INFORMA a los cuidadores/equipo de que puede haber un aumento temporal (estallido de extinción) para prepararlos."}, {"q": "What is a prerequisite to differential reinforcement?", "opts": ["You must try punishment first", "You must conduct a preference assessment", "The learner must have the replacement behavior in their repertoire", "You must identify at least 3 different reinforcers"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El prerrequisito del reforzamiento diferencial: la conducta de reemplazo debe estar EN EL REPERTORIO del cliente para poder reforzarla."}, {"q": "As an RBT you may be asked to conduct indirect assessments and measurements. Which of the following is an example of indirect measurement?", "opts": ["event recording", "interval recording", "surveys", "latency measurment"], "ans": 2, "ex": "La medición INDIRECTA usa encuestas, entrevistas o cuestionarios (lo que otros reportan), no la observación directa."}, {"q": "You are working as a bartender and are training a new bartender how to make a margarita. The steps are: add tequila, add lime, add sweet and sour, add ice, shake, and pour. You first teach the bartender to add the tequila and prompt them through the rest. Once they independently are able to add the tequila you reinforce. You now expect them to add the tequila and the lime independently before receiving reinforcement. What method are you using to teach?", "opts": ["Backwards chaining", "Forward chaining", "Shaping", "Total task chaining"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Enseñar primero 'agregar tequila' y luego exigir más pasos cada vez = ENCADENAMIENTO ADELANTADO (forward chaining), desde el primer paso."}, {"q": "Which of the following is NOT a conditioned reinforcer", "opts": ["sleep", "money", "tokens", "verbal praise"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El sueño es un reforzador INCONDICIONADO (valor biológico). Los condicionados (fichas, dinero, elogios) se aprenden."}, {"q": "Tim is working in a clinic setting. Every day, 4 clients eat lunch at 11am and 4 eat lunch at 12pm. Tim is responsible for taking data on his client's eating behavior, but must also make sure the other clients are eating. Every 3 minutes Tim will look at his client and record whether or not his client is eating. What kind of measurement is this?", "opts": ["Partial interval recording", "Continuous measurement", "Momentary time sampling", "Frequency"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Mirar cada 3 minutos si el cliente está comiendo es muestreo de tiempo MOMENTÁNEO (momentary time sampling)."}, {"q": "Which of the following is NOT an example of an antecedent intervention?", "opts": ["Your son brings home a great report card so you take him out for ice cream", "Your client sometimes scratches you so you wear long sleeves to session", "You withhold all kit kat candy bars from your cilent until session starts", "You're painting your bedroom today, so you spread a bunch of newspaper on the ground to catch the paint drippings"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Tomar helado por SAQUES una buena calificación es una consecuencia (refuerzo), no una intervención de antecedente."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an example of stimulus generalization?", "opts": ["You call your dog multiple nick names throughout the day", "You like to take afternoon naps. Sometimes you nap on the bed, sometimes on the couch, and sometimes on the chair", "You see someone hold up their hand. This sometimes means \"stop\", \"hello\", or \"give me a high five.\"", "When you see your boss in the morning sometimes you say \"hello\", sometimes you say \"good morning\", and sometimes you just smile"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Responder de la misma forma ante estímulos parecidos (generalización de estímulo): el comportamiento 'se generaliza' a contextos similares."}, {"q": "You have been working at a private practice ABA clinic. There is one BCBA who does supervision and runs the business. You are made aware that the BCBA is billing hours they did not actually work. What is your responsibility as an RBT?", "opts": ["Nothing. Billing is not part of your job description", "You can choose whether or not you report your BCBA to the board, but you are not obligated", "You should report your BCBA to the BACB board", "Quit your job immediately"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Si un BCBA factura horas no trabajadas, tu responsabilidad es INFORMAR (en este contexto, reportar al organismo correspondiente como el BACB)."}, {"q": "When producing a line graph the behavior you are tracking goes where?", "opts": ["the x-axis", "on the horizontal", "The y-axis", "on the bottom of the graph"], "ans": 2, "ex": "En el gráfico de línea, el COMPORTAMIENTO que se sigue (frecuencia, duración, etc.) va en el EJE Y. El tiempo va en el X."}, {"q": "You are working in a classroom providing assistance as an RBT. Your client's target behavior is participating in class. Each time your client participates, you give them a check mark. Once the client receives 6 check marks, the client exchange them for either a handful of Skittles or a two minute break. What are you implementing?", "opts": ["Naturalistic teaching", "Forced choice", "negative reinforcement", "Token economy"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Checks que se intercambian por un reforzador (Skittles o descanso) = ECONOMÍA DE FICHAS (token economy)."}, {"q": "When is the best time for you to use an intermittent schedule of reinforcement?", "opts": ["You taught your client a behavior, and now what to maintain that behavior", "Your client is struggling to acquire new skills", "You are trying to teach your client a new behavior", "You are struggling to gain momentum with a client"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El refuerzo INTERMITENTE se usa cuando la conducta YA está establecida, para MANTENERLA y hacerla resistente a la extinción."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an example of automatic negative reinforcement?", "opts": ["You are driving in your brand new car on a perfect Spring time day. Your favorite song comes on the radio, so you turn it up louder", "Your client is constantly receiving detention at school. During an observation you notice that every time your client disrupts the class, his friends laugh", "You were making coffee when you accidentally dropped the pot. The pot shattered, and glass went everywhere. You ask your roommate to help you clean it up, which they do", "You went out with your friends last night, and woke up with a massive headache. You take Tylenol and your headache goes away"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Dolor de cabeza → te tomas Tylenol → se quita: la conducta elimina el estímulo aversivo AUTOMÁTICAMENTE = reforzamiento negativo automático."}, {"q": "You are assigned a client in-home. The client has multiple siblings, but they all share one Xbox. Your BCBA requests that you spend your first two sessions building rapport, and observing behavior. You notice that each time your client's brother is on the Xbox, your client will run over and unplug the Xbox. This results in the brother getting off of the Xbox and your client playing the Xbox. What would you hypothesize is the function of unplugging the Xbox?", "opts": ["tangible", "attention", "automatic", "escape"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Desenchufar el Xbox le da ACCESO a la consola (el hermano se baja): función TANGIBLE."}, {"q": "Your client is learning how to prepare dinner for his family. He recently learned to cook spaghetti and meatballs independently except for boiling the water and adding seasoning. What method would be best to teach your client these steps?", "opts": ["Backwards chaining", "Total task chaining", "DTT", "Forward chaining"], "ans": 1, "ex": "El cliente ya domina casi toda la cadena; solo enseñas los pasos que falla (hervir agua y sazonar) = encadenamiento por tarea total."}, {"q": "This differential reinforcement relies on the absence of a behavior", "opts": ["DRO", "DRL", "DRA", "DRI"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El DRO refuerza la AUSENCIA de la conducta objetivo (por un periodo). Es diferencia con DRA (alternativa) y DRI (incompatible)."}, {"q": "You are working with a client in-home. Your client's grandma and grandpa live with the family, and your client has a very good relationship with their grandparents. One day, the grandma gets sick and is admitted to the hospital. What should you do?", "opts": ["Give your client two weeks off out of respect for the family", "Nothing. Continue running your sessions as usual", "Visit your client on your off-days for extra support", "Report this to your BCBA and make a note of it in your session notes"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Mantén la relación profesional y apoya a la familia dentro de tus funciones; NO asumas cuidados personales ni cruces el límite profesional."}, {"q": "Select the best definition for differential reinforcement, from the choices below:", "opts": ["A stimulus that, when presented following a behavior, causes an overall DECREASE in that behavior over time", "A stimulus, that when presented following a bx, causes an overall INCREASE in that bx over time", "A stimulus change that signals the availability of a reinforcer", "Providing greater reinforcement for better approximations of a target behavior, and placing other behaviors on extinction or on a less desirable reinforcement schedule"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El reforzamiento diferencial: refuerzas una respuesta o clase de respuestas y NO refuerzas otra. Así una aumenta y la otra se reduce."}, {"q": "Which of the following is known as the ordinate?", "opts": ["condition change line", "y-axis", "baseline", "x-axis"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La ORDENADA es el eje Y (la conducta). La abscisa es el eje X."}, {"q": "Whenever your client wants to get up from the table they will bang their fists and scream. Your BCBA decides it's time to intervene on this behavior. You and the BCBA collaborate on a treatment plan. Before implementation, your BCBA advises the parents that the client might bang their firsts harder and scream louder at first. What is your BCBA referring to?", "opts": ["An extinction burst", "Punishment induced aggression", "Resistance to punishment", "Unintended side effects of extinction"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Que la conducta empeore al inicio al retirar el refuerzo es el ESTALLIDO DE EXTINCIÓN. Es esperado; se avisa a los padres para normalizarlo."}, {"q": "Which of the following best describes response latency?", "opts": ["The time between the waiter asking you what you would like to order, and you completing your order", "The time between the waiter asking you what you would like to order, and you starting to tell the waiter your order", "The time in between you sitting down for dinner, and then leaving dinner", "The time in between bites of food once you receive your order"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Latencia de respuesta: tiempo entre el SD (el mesero pregunta) y el COMIENZO de tu respuesta (empezar a decir tu pedido)."}, {"q": "Tammy wants to go to a party this weekend. Her mom tells Tiffany that if her homework is done when mom gets home from work, she is allowed to go to the party. What would be the best way for mom to measure this goal?", "opts": ["Frequency count of how many problems Tammy does", "Setting up cameras to record Tammy completing her homework", "Permanent Product", "Event recording"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Para medir si 'hizo la tarea', la madre puede revisar el TRABAJO TERMINADO: es un producto permanente (verificar al llegar de trabajar)."}, {"q": "Each month an RBT must receive supervision of _____ of their hours spent providing services", "opts": ["15%", "2%", "5%", "10%"], "ans": 2, "ex": "El RBT recibe supervisión del 5% de sus horas cada mes."}, {"q": "Bill, a fifth grade special education teacher, brings in a bowl of candy for his students. He tells his students they must first complete their quizzes before they are allowed to eat their candy. What is Bill implementing?", "opts": ["A contingency", "Incidental teaching", "DTT", "Prompting"], "ans": 0, "ex": "'Primero terminar el examen, luego dulces' es una contingencia: si ocurre la conducta, entonces viene la consecuencia."}, {"q": "Which of the following is the best example of imitation?", "opts": ["Yesterday you read morning announcements. Today, Kevin reads morning announcements", "You tell your client \"say blue\" and your client says blue", "At 8am you and your roommates leave for your class that starts at 9am", "You prepare a special meal by pulling up a YouTube video and copying the cooking instructor's actions"], "ans": 3, "ex": "La imitación: copiar las ACCIONES de otro (seguir al instructor de cocina del video). El modelo es la acción, no palabras."}, {"q": "Differential reinforcement leads to ______?", "opts": ["Discrimination", "Prompting", "Incidental teaching", "Shaping"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El reforzamiento diferencial lleva a la DISCRIMINACIÓN: el cliente aprende a responder solo donde hay refuerzo."}, {"q": "During long car rides, Billy would tap on the window several times in a row. Billy's mom decided to buy him an Ipad for car rides. Now, when they take car rides, Billy's mom gives Billy the ipad which provides Billy with automatic reinforcement. Billy no longer taps on the window. This is an example of?", "opts": ["DRI", "DRO", "DRD", "DRA"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Billy deja de tocarlo porque recibe una alternativa para la misma función (el iPad) = reforzamiento diferencial de conducta INCOMPATIBLE (DRI)."}, {"q": "Which of the following is the best method for identifying the function of a behavior?", "opts": ["Functional analysis", "Functional behavior assessment", "Indirect assessment", "Direct assessment"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El mejor método para identificar la función es el análisis FUNCIONAL (manipular condiciones y observar efectos)."}, {"q": "You have been working with a family for over a year now. One day, the mom tells you about a new Netflix documentary she watched that claimed autism can be cured by eating frozen peas every single day. She asks your opinion. What should you do?", "opts": ["Tell your client they are crazy to believe that theory", "Politely decline to give your opinion and refer your client to the supervisor", "Watch the Netflix documentary first, and then share your opinion on this diet", "Report your client to the authorities"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Dieta 'milagrosa' del documental: no des tu opinión personal; refiere a la familia a la BCBA/supervisor (ciencia y ética)."}, {"q": "You and your friends are watching the Super Bowl. A commercial advertising Taco Bell's new Gordita Crunch is shown. You all suddenly agree that you have to go get Taco Bell at half time. The commercial functions as a _____?", "opts": ["MO", "SD", "Consequence", "Prompt"], "ans": 0, "ex": "El anuncio de Taco Bell AUMENTA el valor de ir a comer y evoca la conducta de querer ir: es una operación motivadora (MO)."}, {"q": "Frequency and rate are often used interchangeably in behavior analysis. What is the distinction between the two?", "opts": ["Rate measures how long something occurred, while frequency measures how many times something occurred", "Rate is an indirect measurement", "Rate is frequency with a time component added", "There is no difference between the two"], "ans": 2, "ex": "La RASÓN (rate) es la frecuencia con componente de TIEMPO (por hora/minuto). Frecuencia es solo el número."}, {"q": "You are planning a trip with your group of friends. You start a group chat with everyone in it. Your phone vibrates every 1 to 3 minutes. What schedule matches the schedule of your phone vibrating?", "opts": ["FI2", "FR2", "VR2", "VI2"], "ans": 3, "ex": "El teléfono vibra cada 1-3 minutos (intervalos variables) = programa de intervalo VARIABLE (VI2, promedio ~2 min)."}, {"q": "Which of the following is an example of response generalization?", "opts": ["You teach your client to wash their hands at home. Your client can now wash their hands at Target, Wendy's, and school", "You are staying over at a friend's house for the weekend. They ask you to not use the white towels, so you use the green towels instead", "You receive a text message that says \"what's up.\" Sometimes you respond \"nothing much, you?\" Sometimes you respond \"working.\" and sometimes you respond \"bored. Want to hang out?\"", "You are teaching your client how to multiply. You ask \"what is 2x2\" and then you say \"4\". Your client responds with \"4\""], "ans": 2, "ex": "Responder 'qué hay' de varias formas distintas para la misma persona = generalización de RESPUESTA (variedad de respuestas que funcionan)."}, {"q": "Which of the following is NOT an example of a punishment?", "opts": ["Louis continues to disrupt the class. Every time he does, the teacher yells at him and says \"I'm going to send you to timeout.\"", "Joe missed his curfew last night, so his parents took away his car keys. Joe no longer misses curfew", "Tammy buys soup from the deli. When she gets home, she pours the soup in a bowl, and microwaves the soup in the bowl. When she takes the bowl out, she burns her hand. She no longer uses that bowl", "Bobby answers three questions correctly in a row. The teacher says \"great job, Bobby!\" Bobby's friends start laughing at him. He stops answering questions"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Decir 'gran trabajo' por 3 respuestas correctas REFUERZA la conducta: es refuerzo, NO castigo. Es la opción que NO es un castigo."}, {"q": "Your client has difficulty discriminating between different items, and will always choose an item to their left when presented with choices. What type of preference assessment is most appropriate?", "opts": ["Single stimulus", "Forced choice", "Multiple stimulus without replacement", "Multiple stimulus with replacement"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Como el cliente elige siempre el de la izquierda, usar presentación de UN SOLO estímulo a la vez evita el sesgo de posición."}, {"q": "You are assigned to a BCBA to assist in an assessment for a brand new client. During the course of the assessment, you ask your client \"say your name\", \"give me a high five\", \"what is 2+2\", and several other basic questions. What are you doing?", "opts": ["Naturalistic Teaching", "DTT", "Shaping", "Probing"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Pedir 'di tu nombre', 'choca esos cinco', '¿cuánto es 2+2?' es SONDEO/probing: preguntar para ver qué conductas ya existen."}, {"q": "After 3 months of teaching, your client is finally able to tell you their name and their address. You are really excited, and want to show their parents. When the client's mom asks \"what is your address?\", your client is unable to answer. This is a failure to ______?", "opts": ["Shape", "Maintain", "Prompt", "Generalize"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Sabe su nombre/dirección contigo pero NO con su mamá: fracaso de generalización de estímulo (no se generaliza al SD de la mamá)."}, {"q": "Which of the following is the best example of interresponse time?", "opts": ["Flights were too expensive, so you decided you would drive to the beach instead. The trip took 4 hours there, and 5 hours back", "You got to the party at 8pm, but you didn't start to greet your friends until 8:10 pm", "You are mailing out wedding invitations. You have to lick and seal 300 envelopes. You usually take a 10 second break in between sealing one and licking another", "You are measuring on-task behavior. If your client stays on task the entire time, you mark it as correct"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Los 10 segundos entre sellar una y lamer otra = IRT (tiempo entre respuestas)."}, {"q": "Which of the following best represents least-to-most prompting?", "opts": ["partial physical -> full physical -> verbal prompt", "modeling -> gestural -> verbal", "visual -> modeling -> verbal", "verbal -> gestural -> modeling"], "ans": 3, "ex": "De menos a más intrusivo: verbal → gestual → modelado → físico. Eso es desvanecimiento DE MENOS A MÁS (least-to-most)."}, {"q": "You are teaching someone how to shoot pool. You start by holding their arms and demonstrating the motion. You then only put your hands on their elbows. You then remove the prompt all together. What are you implementing?", "opts": ["Least-to-most prompting", "Task chaining", "Delayed prompting", "Gradual guidance"], "ans": 3, "ex": "Guiar con las manos y retirar gradualmente el contacto (brazos → codos → nada) es guía FÍSICA GRADUAL (gradual guidance)."}, {"q": "Continuous reinforcement is also known as ____?", "opts": ["An FR1 schedule", "the best way to maintain a behavior", "A FI1 schedule", "The opposite of intermittent reinforcement"], "ans": 0, "ex": "Refuerzo continuo = cada respuesta correcta = programa FR1 (razón fija 1)."}, {"q": "When you are speaking with a family it is important to ____?", "opts": ["Document every conversation you have with the parents", "Avoid using jargon and technical language", "Use as much technical ABA language as you can. It's important for the family to understand the terms", "avoid speaking to the family as much as possible. Your job is only to implement treatment plans"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Al hablar con la familia, EVITA la jerga y el lenguaje técnico: usa términos claros que todos entiendan."}, {"q": "Your client hates the sound of Baby Shark being played through your phone. Whenever you play Baby Shark, your client hits you. You teach your client to say \"please stop playing that song\" instead of hitting you. Now, when your client says \"please stop playing that song\" you stop playing the song, but when your client hits you, you continue playing the song. What is this considered?", "opts": ["DRI", "DRO", "DRA", "DRH"], "ans": 2, "ex": "Enseñas el PEDIDO verbal; cuando golpea, la canción continúa (sin refuerzo) y cuando pide, se detiene: reforzamiento diferencial de ALTERNATIVA (DRA)."}, {"q": "What is the ultimate goal of reinforcement?", "opts": ["A self-management plan", "That the client will receive reinforcement from the natural environment", "Fade to a VR schedule", "A behavior contract"], "ans": 1, "ex": "La meta final del reforzamiento es la CONDUCTA CAMBIADA y sostenida (mantenimiento en el tiempo y en otros entornos), no solo el ensayo inmediato."}, {"q": "A consequence intervention is also known as a _____ strategy?", "opts": ["punishment", "reactive", "unethical", "proactive"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Una intervención de consecuencia (reforzamiento o castigo) se llama estrategia CONSECUENTE (consequence-based)."}, {"q": "Your partner makes the same terrible joke every time you bring home Starbucks. In the past, you laughed only to be nice and the jokes continued. Today, you decided you weren't going to laugh or respond anymore. What are you implementing?", "opts": ["Negative punishment", "Extinction", "Positive punishment", "Extinction burst"], "ans": 1, "ex": "Ya no reír ni responder ante el chiste (retiras el refuerzo que lo mantenía) es EXTINCIÓN, aunque el socio piense que fue mala educación."}], "count": 80}];